---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsSchedulesRequest
---@field maxConcurrentRunCount? string Required. Maximum number of runs that can be started concurrently for this Schedule. This is the limit for starting the scheduled requests and not the execution of the operations/jobs created by the requests (if applicable).
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was updated.
---@field name? string Immutable. The resource name of the Schedule.
---@field displayName? string Required. User provided name of the Schedule. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field catchUp? boolean Output only. Whether to backfill missed runs when the schedule is resumed from PAUSED state. If set to true, all missed runs will be scheduled. New runs will be scheduled after the backfill is complete. Default to false.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was created.
---@field lastScheduledRunResponse? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ScheduleRunResponse Output only. Response of the last scheduled run. This is the response for starting the scheduled requests and not the execution of the operations/jobs created by the requests (if applicable). Unset if no run has been scheduled yet.
---@field createNotebookExecutionJobRequest? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1CreateNotebookExecutionJobRequest Request for NotebookService.CreateNotebookExecutionJob.
---@field maxConcurrentActiveRunCount? string Optional. Specifies the maximum number of active runs that can be executed concurrently for this Schedule. This limits the number of runs that can be in a non-terminal state at the same time. Currently, this field is only supported for requests of type CreatePipelineJobRequest.
---@field cron? string Cron schedule (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cron) to launch scheduled runs. To explicitly set a timezone to the cron tab, apply a prefix in the cron tab: "CRON_TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}" or "TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}". The ${IANA_TIME_ZONE} may only be a valid string from IANA time zone database. For example, "CRON_TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *", or "TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *".
---@field endTime? string Optional. Timestamp after which no new runs can be scheduled. If specified, The schedule will be completed when either end_time is reached or when scheduled_run_count >= max_run_count. If not specified, new runs will keep getting scheduled until this Schedule is paused or deleted. Already scheduled runs will be allowed to complete. Unset if not specified.
---@field lastResumeTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was last resumed. Unset if never resumed from pause.
---@field maxRunCount? string Optional. Maximum run count of the schedule. If specified, The schedule will be completed when either started_run_count >= max_run_count or when end_time is reached. If not specified, new runs will keep getting scheduled until this Schedule is paused or deleted. Already scheduled runs will be allowed to complete. Unset if not specified.
---@field allowQueueing? boolean Optional. Whether new scheduled runs can be queued when max_concurrent_runs limit is reached. If set to true, new runs will be queued instead of skipped. Default to false.
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ScheduleStateEnum|string Output only. The state of this Schedule.
---@field startTime? string Optional. Timestamp after which the first run can be scheduled. Default to Schedule create time if not specified.
---@field nextRunTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule should schedule the next run. Having a next_run_time in the past means the runs are being started behind schedule.
---@field startedRunCount? string Output only. The number of runs started by this schedule.
---@field lastPauseTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was last paused. Unset if never paused.
---@field createPipelineJobRequest? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1CreatePipelineJobRequest Request for PipelineService.CreatePipelineJob. CreatePipelineJobRequest.parent field is required (format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}).
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Location to create the Schedule in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsSemanticGovernancePoliciesRequest
---@field agent? string Required. The name of the agent in Agent Registry that is affected by this policy. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent}`
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this SemanticGovernancePolicy was created.
---@field name? string Identifier. Resource name of the SemanticGovernancePolicy.
---@field agentIdentity? string Output only. Represents the principal of the agent, used by the Policy Decision Point (PDP) for governance checks. For more information, see https://docs.cloud.google.com/agent-builder/agent-engine/agent-identity Format: `principal://TRUST_DOMAIN/NAMESPACE/AGENT_NAME` Example: `principal://agents.global.org-ORGANIZATION_ID.system.id.goog/resources/aiplatform/projects/PROJECT_NUMBER/locations/LOCATION/reasoningEngines/AGENT_ENGINE_ID`
---@field displayName? string Optional. The user-defined name of the SemanticGovernancePolicy.
---@field naturalLanguageConstraint? string Required. The natural language constraint of the SemanticGovernancePolicy.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this SemanticGovernancePolicy was last updated.
---@field agentResponseCustomization? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentResponseCustomization Optional. Settings for customizing the agent's response to end users when this policy is evaluated, such as messages displayed when the policy denies a request.
---@field etag? string Optional. Used to perform consistent read-modify-write transactions. If provided, the request will only succeed if the etag matches the current value. Otherwise, an ABORTED error will be returned.
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the SemanticGovernancePolicy.
---@field dryRun? boolean Optional. If true, this policy is evaluated and its result is reported, but the policy is not enforced: a violation does not block the agent's action. Use this to validate a policy against real traffic before turning enforcement on. Defaults to `false`, meaning the policy is enforced. This setting applies only to this policy. If the SemanticGovernancePolicyEngine for the project is itself in dry run, every policy behaves as dry run regardless of this field.
---@field mcpTools? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1SemanticGovernancePolicyMcpToolList Optional. The McpTools that are affected by this policy.
---@field semanticGovernancePolicyId? string Required. The ID to use for the SemanticGovernancePolicy, which will become the final component of the SemanticGovernancePolicy's resource name. This value may be up to 63 characters, and valid characters are `[a-z0-9-]`. The first character cannot be a number or hyphen. The last character must be a letter or a number.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Location into which to create the SemanticGovernancePolicy. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsServingProfilesRequest
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when the ServingProfile was created.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the ServingProfile. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the ServingProfile.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when the ServingProfile was last updated.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the ServingProfile.
---@field cmekConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ServingProfileCmekConfig CMEK configuration for the ServingProfile.
---@field scope? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ServingProfileScopeEnum|string Required. The specific API this ServingProfile applies to.
---@field servingProfileId? string Required. The ID to use for the ServingProfile, which will become the final component of the ServingProfile's resource name. This value should be 1-63 characters, and valid characters are `^[a-z]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?$`.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Location to create the ServingProfile in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsSpecialistPoolsRequest
---@field name? string Required. The resource name of the SpecialistPool.
---@field specialistManagerEmails? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList The email addresses of the managers in the SpecialistPool.
---@field displayName? string Required. The user-defined name of the SpecialistPool. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters. This field should be unique on project-level.
---@field specialistManagersCount? number Output only. The number of managers in this SpecialistPool.
---@field pendingDataLabelingJobs? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Output only. The resource name of the pending data labeling jobs.
---@field specialistWorkerEmails? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList The email addresses of workers in the SpecialistPool.
---@field parent string Required. The parent Project name for the new SpecialistPool. The form is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`.

---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsStudiesRequest
---@field inactiveReason? string Output only. A human readable reason why the Study is inactive. This should be empty if a study is ACTIVE or COMPLETED.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time at which the study was created.
---@field studySpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1StudySpec Required. Configuration of the Study.
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1StudyStateEnum|string Output only. The detailed state of a Study.
---@field name? string Output only. The name of a study. The study's globally unique identifier. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/studies/{study}`
---@field displayName? string Required. Describes the Study, default value is empty string.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Location to create the CustomJob in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsStudiesTrialsRequest
---@field webAccessUris? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap Output only. URIs for accessing [interactive shells](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/training/monitor-debug-interactive-shell) (one URI for each training node). Only available if this trial is part of a HyperparameterTuningJob and the job's trial_job_spec.enable_web_access field is `true`. The keys are names of each node used for the trial; for example, `workerpool0-0` for the primary node, `workerpool1-0` for the first node in the second worker pool, and `workerpool1-1` for the second node in the second worker pool. The values are the URIs for each node's interactive shell.
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1TrialStateEnum|string Output only. The detailed state of the Trial.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Time when the Trial was started.
---@field customJob? string Output only. The CustomJob name linked to the Trial. It's set for a HyperparameterTuningJob's Trial.
---@field id? string Output only. The identifier of the Trial assigned by the service.
---@field finalMeasurement? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Measurement Output only. The final measurement containing the objective value.
---@field infeasibleReason? string Output only. A human readable string describing why the Trial is infeasible. This is set only if Trial state is `INFEASIBLE`.
---@field parameters? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1TrialParameterList Output only. The parameters of the Trial.
---@field measurements? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1MeasurementList Output only. A list of measurements that are strictly lexicographically ordered by their induced tuples (steps, elapsed_duration). These are used for early stopping computations.
---@field endTime? string Output only. Time when the Trial's status changed to `SUCCEEDED` or `INFEASIBLE`.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the Trial assigned by the service.
---@field clientId? string Output only. The identifier of the client that originally requested this Trial. Each client is identified by a unique client_id. When a client asks for a suggestion, Vertex AI Vizier will assign it a Trial. The client should evaluate the Trial, complete it, and report back to Vertex AI Vizier. If suggestion is asked again by same client_id before the Trial is completed, the same Trial will be returned. Multiple clients with different client_ids can ask for suggestions simultaneously, each of them will get their own Trial.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Study to create the Trial in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/studies/{study}`

---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsTensorboardsExperimentsRequest
---@field displayName? string User provided name of this TensorboardExperiment.
---@field description? string Description of this TensorboardExperiment.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your TensorboardExperiment. Label keys and values cannot be longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one Dataset (System labels are excluded). See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with `aiplatform.googleapis.com/` and are immutable. The following system labels exist for each Dataset: * `aiplatform.googleapis.com/dataset_metadata_schema`: output only. Its value is the metadata_schema's title.
---@field source? string Immutable. Source of the TensorboardExperiment. Example: a custom training job.
---@field name? string Output only. Name of the TensorboardExperiment. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tensorboards/{tensorboard}/experiments/{experiment}`
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this TensorboardExperiment was last updated.
---@field etag? string Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this TensorboardExperiment was created.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Tensorboard to create the TensorboardExperiment in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tensorboards/{tensorboard}`
---@field tensorboardExperimentId? string Required. The ID to use for the Tensorboard experiment, which becomes the final component of the Tensorboard experiment's resource name. This value should be 1-128 characters, and valid characters are `/a-z-/`.

---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsTensorboardsExperimentsRunsRequest
---@field displayName? string Required. User provided name of this TensorboardRun. This value must be unique among all TensorboardRuns belonging to the same parent TensorboardExperiment.
---@field description? string Description of this TensorboardRun.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this TensorboardRun was last updated.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your TensorboardRuns. This field will be used to filter and visualize Runs in the Tensorboard UI. For example, a Vertex AI training job can set a label aiplatform.googleapis.com/training_job_id=xxxxx to all the runs created within that job. An end user can set a label experiment_id=xxxxx for all the runs produced in a Jupyter notebook. These runs can be grouped by a label value and visualized together in the Tensorboard UI. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one TensorboardRun (System labels are excluded). See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this TensorboardRun was created.
---@field name? string Output only. Name of the TensorboardRun. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tensorboards/{tensorboard}/experiments/{experiment}/runs/{run}`
---@field etag? string Used to perform a consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field tensorboardRunId? string Required. The ID to use for the Tensorboard run, which becomes the final component of the Tensorboard run's resource name. This value should be 1-128 characters, and valid characters are `/a-z-/`.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the TensorboardExperiment to create the TensorboardRun in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tensorboards/{tensorboard}/experiments/{experiment}`

---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsTensorboardsExperimentsRunsTimeSeriesRequest
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this TensorboardTimeSeries was last updated.
---@field etag? string Used to perform a consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field description? string Description of this TensorboardTimeSeries.
---@field valueType? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1TensorboardTimeSeriesValueTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. Type of TensorboardTimeSeries value.
---@field pluginName? string Immutable. Name of the plugin this time series pertain to. Such as Scalar, Tensor, Blob
---@field pluginData? string Data of the current plugin, with the size limited to 65KB.
---@field name? string Output only. Name of the TensorboardTimeSeries.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this TensorboardTimeSeries was created.
---@field displayName? string Required. User provided name of this TensorboardTimeSeries. This value should be unique among all TensorboardTimeSeries resources belonging to the same TensorboardRun resource (parent resource).
---@field metadata? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1TensorboardTimeSeriesMetadata Output only. Scalar, Tensor, or Blob metadata for this TensorboardTimeSeries.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the TensorboardRun to create the TensorboardTimeSeries in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tensorboards/{tensorboard}/experiments/{experiment}/runs/{run}`
---@field tensorboardTimeSeriesId? string Optional. The user specified unique ID to use for the TensorboardTimeSeries, which becomes the final component of the TensorboardTimeSeries's resource name. This value should match "a-z0-9{0, 127}"

---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsTensorboardsRequest
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key spec for a Tensorboard. If set, this Tensorboard and all sub-resources of this Tensorboard will be secured by this key.
---@field blobStoragePathPrefix? string Output only. Consumer project Cloud Storage path prefix used to store blob data, which can either be a bucket or directory. Does not end with a '/'.
---@field runCount? number Output only. The number of Runs stored in this Tensorboard.
---@field etag? string Used to perform a consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field isDefault? boolean Used to indicate if the TensorBoard instance is the default one. Each project & region can have at most one default TensorBoard instance. Creation of a default TensorBoard instance and updating an existing TensorBoard instance to be default will mark all other TensorBoard instances (if any) as non default.
---@field description? string Description of this Tensorboard.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Tensorboard was last updated.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your Tensorboards. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one Tensorboard (System labels are excluded). See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable.
---@field name? string Output only. Name of the Tensorboard. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tensorboards/{tensorboard}`
---@field displayName? string Required. User provided name of this Tensorboard.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Tensorboard was created.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Location to create the Tensorboard in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsTrainingPipelinesRequest
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when the TrainingPipeline was created.
---@field trainingTaskDefinition? string Required. A Google Cloud Storage path to the YAML file that defines the training task which is responsible for producing the model artifact, and may also include additional auxiliary work. The definition files that can be used here are found in gs://google-cloud-aiplatform/schema/trainingjob/definition/. Note: The URI given on output will be immutable and probably different, including the URI scheme, than the one given on input. The output URI will point to a location where the user only has a read access.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time when the TrainingPipeline was most recently updated.
---@field modelToUpload? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Model Describes the Model that may be uploaded (via ModelService.UploadModel) by this TrainingPipeline. The TrainingPipeline's training_task_definition should make clear whether this Model description should be populated, and if there are any special requirements regarding how it should be filled. If nothing is mentioned in the training_task_definition, then it should be assumed that this field should not be filled and the training task either uploads the Model without a need of this information, or that training task does not support uploading a Model as part of the pipeline. When the Pipeline's state becomes `PIPELINE_STATE_SUCCEEDED` and the trained Model had been uploaded into Vertex AI, then the model_to_upload's resource name is populated. The Model is always uploaded into the Project and Location in which this pipeline is.
---@field error? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Only populated when the pipeline's state is `PIPELINE_STATE_FAILED` or `PIPELINE_STATE_CANCELLED`.
---@field inputDataConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1InputDataConfig Specifies Vertex AI owned input data that may be used for training the Model. The TrainingPipeline's training_task_definition should make clear whether this config is used and if there are any special requirements on how it should be filled. If nothing about this config is mentioned in the training_task_definition, then it should be assumed that the TrainingPipeline does not depend on this configuration.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key spec for a TrainingPipeline. If set, this TrainingPipeline will be secured by this key. Note: Model trained by this TrainingPipeline is also secured by this key if model_to_upload is not set separately.
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1TrainingPipelineStateEnum|string Output only. The detailed state of the pipeline.
---@field modelId? string Optional. The ID to use for the uploaded Model, which will become the final component of the model resource name. This value may be up to 63 characters, and valid characters are `[a-z0-9_-]`. The first character cannot be a number or hyphen.
---@field displayName? string Required. The user-defined name of this TrainingPipeline.
---@field endTime? string Output only. Time when the TrainingPipeline entered any of the following states: `PIPELINE_STATE_SUCCEEDED`, `PIPELINE_STATE_FAILED`, `PIPELINE_STATE_CANCELLED`.
---@field parentModel? string Optional. When specify this field, the `model_to_upload` will not be uploaded as a new model, instead, it will become a new version of this `parent_model`.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the TrainingPipeline.
---@field trainingTaskInputs? any Required. The training task's parameter(s), as specified in the training_task_definition's `inputs`.
---@field trainingTaskMetadata? any Output only. The metadata information as specified in the training_task_definition's `metadata`. This metadata is an auxiliary runtime and final information about the training task. While the pipeline is running this information is populated only at a best effort basis. Only present if the pipeline's training_task_definition contains `metadata` object.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Time when the TrainingPipeline for the first time entered the `PIPELINE_STATE_RUNNING` state.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize TrainingPipelines. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Location to create the TrainingPipeline in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsTuningJobsRequest
---@field baseModel? string The base model that is being tuned. See [Supported models](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/model-reference/tuning#supported_models).
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the TuningJob.
---@field experiment? string Output only. The Experiment associated with this TuningJob.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time when the TuningJob was most recently updated.
---@field preTunedModel? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PreTunedModel The pre-tuned model for continuous tuning.
---@field serviceAccount? string The service account that the tuningJob workload runs as. If not specified, the Vertex AI Secure Fine-Tuned Service Agent in the project will be used. See https://cloud.google.com/iam/docs/service-agents#vertex-ai-secure-fine-tuning-service-agent Users starting the pipeline must have the `iam.serviceAccounts.actAs` permission on this service account.
---@field tunedModelDisplayName? string Optional. The display name of the TunedModel. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters. For continuous tuning, tuned_model_display_name will by default use the same display name as the pre-tuned model. If a new display name is provided, the tuning job will create a new model instead of a new version.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap Optional. The labels with user-defined metadata to organize TuningJob and generated resources such as Model and Endpoint. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when the TuningJob was created.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key options for a TuningJob. If this is set, then all resources created by the TuningJob will be encrypted with the provided encryption key.
---@field gcsMetricsUri? string Output only. The Cloud Storage metrics URI associated with this TuningJob.
---@field error? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Only populated when job's state is `JOB_STATE_FAILED` or `JOB_STATE_CANCELLED`.
---@field tuningDataStats? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1TuningDataStats Output only. The tuning data statistics associated with this TuningJob.
---@field tunedModel? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1TunedModel Output only. The tuned model resources associated with this TuningJob.
---@field preferenceOptimizationSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PreferenceOptimizationSpec Tuning Spec for Preference Optimization.
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1TuningJobStateEnum|string Output only. The detailed state of the job.
---@field endTime? string Output only. Time when the TuningJob entered any of the following JobStates: `JOB_STATE_SUCCEEDED`, `JOB_STATE_FAILED`, `JOB_STATE_CANCELLED`, `JOB_STATE_EXPIRED`.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Time when the TuningJob for the first time entered the `JOB_STATE_RUNNING` state.
---@field name? string Output only. Identifier. Resource name of a TuningJob. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tuningJobs/{tuning_job}`
---@field evaluateDatasetRuns? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluateDatasetRunList Output only. Evaluation runs for the Tuning Job.
---@field supervisedTuningSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1SupervisedTuningSpec Tuning Spec for Supervised Fine Tuning.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the location to create the tuning job in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

