---Represents configuration for an Agent.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentConfig
---@field description? string Optional. A high-level description of the agent's role and responsibilities. Critical for evaluating if the agent is routing tasks correctly.
---@field subAgents? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. The list of valid agent IDs that this agent can delegate to. This defines the directed edges in the multi-agent system graph topology.
---@field tools? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ToolList Optional. The list of tools available to this agent.
---@field agentId? string Required. Unique identifier of the agent. This ID is used to refer to this agent, e.g., in AgentEvent.author, or in the `sub_agents` field. It must be unique within the `agents` map.
---@field agentType? string Optional. The type or class of the agent (e.g., "LlmAgent", "RouterAgent", "ToolUseAgent"). Useful for the autorater to understand the expected behavior of the agent.
---@field instruction? string Optional. Provides instructions for the LLM model, guiding the agent's behavior. Can be static or dynamic. Dynamic instructions can contain placeholders like {variable_name} that will be resolved at runtime using the `AgentEvent.state_delta` field.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentConfigMap { [string]: gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentConfig }

---Represents data specific to multi-turn agent evaluations.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentData
---@field turns? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ConversationTurnList Optional. A chronological list of conversation turns. Each turn represents a logical execution cycle (e.g., User Input -> Agent Response).
---@field agents? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentConfigMap Optional. A map containing the static configurations for each agent in the system. Key: agent_id (matches the `author` field in events). Value: The static configuration of the agent.

---Represents a single event in the execution trace.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentEvent
---@field eventTime? string Optional. The timestamp when the event occurred.
---@field stateDelta? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentMap Optional. The change in the session state caused by this event. This is a key-value map of fields that were modified or added by the event.
---@field content? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Content Required. The content of the event (e.g., text response, tool call, tool response).
---@field activeTools? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ToolList Optional. The list of tools that were active/available to the agent at the time of this event. This overrides the `AgentConfig.tools` if set.
---@field author? string Required. The ID of the agent or entity that generated this event. Use "user" to denote events generated by the end-user.

