---The transcription of an audio part. For multi-speaker audio, each speaker segment is a separate `Part` with its own `AudioTranscription` carrying the `speaker_label`.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AudioTranscription
---@field speakerLabel? string Optional. A label identifying the speaker of this audio segment (e.g. `spk_1`, `spk_2`). Present when `diarization` is set.
---@field text? string Required. The transcription text of this audio segment.
---@field words? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AudioTranscriptionWordInfoList Optional. Detailed word-level transcriptions and timing details. Present when `word_timestamp` is set.

---Configuration for speech recognition (transcription).
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AudioTranscriptionConfig
---@field customVocabulary? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. A list of custom vocabulary phrases to bias the speech recognition model toward recognizing specific terms.
---@field languageCodes? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. BCP-47 language codes providing hints about the languages present in the audio. If omitted or empty, defaults to automatic language detection.
---@field languageAuto? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AudioTranscriptionConfigLanguageAuto Optional. Deprecated: Use top-level `language_codes` instead. The model will detect the language automatically.
---@field wordTimestamp? boolean Optional. Configures word-level timestamp generation.
---@field mode? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AudioTranscriptionConfigModeEnum|string Optional. Configures transcription mode. Supported values: `VERBATIM`, `SMART`. If unspecified, defaults to `VERBATIM` transcription. In `SMART` mode, the model performs disfluency removal (eliminating filler words, repetitions, and false starts), light grammatical cleanup, automatic formatting (paragraphs, bullet points, numbered lists), and minor user edits (inline self-corrections). Timestamps and diarization are incompatible with mode `SMART`.
---@field diarization? boolean Optional. Configures speaker diarization.
---@field adaptationPhrases? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. Deprecated: Use `custom_vocabulary` instead. A list of phrases to bias the speech recognition model towards.
---@field sourceText? string Optional. The source text to be edited or rewritten via voice instructions. When provided in `SMART` mode, the model evaluates the audio input against this text and emits the complete replacement text in the candidate response rather than appending to it.
---@field languageHints? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AudioTranscriptionConfigLanguageHints Optional. Deprecated: Use top-level `language_codes` instead. Specifies one or more languages in the audio.

---Deprecated: Use top-level `language_codes` instead. Indicates the language of the audio should be automatically detected.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AudioTranscriptionConfigLanguageAuto

---Deprecated: Use top-level `language_codes` instead. Provides hints to the model about possible languages present in the audio.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AudioTranscriptionConfigLanguageHints
---@field languageCodes? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Required. Deprecated: Use top-level `language_codes` instead. BCP-47 language codes. At least one must be specified.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AudioTranscriptionConfigModeEnum "MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"VERBATIM"|"SMART"

