---True positive, false positive, or false negative. EvaluatedAnnotation is only available under ModelEvaluationSlice with slice of `annotationSpec` dimension.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluatedAnnotation
---@field errorAnalysisAnnotations? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ErrorAnalysisAnnotationList Annotations of model error analysis results.
---@field explanations? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluatedAnnotationExplanationList Explanations of predictions. Each element of the explanations indicates the explanation for one explanation Method. The attributions list in the EvaluatedAnnotationExplanation.explanation object corresponds to the predictions list. For example, the second element in the attributions list explains the second element in the predictions list.
---@field predictions? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentList Output only. The model predicted annotations. For true positive, there is one and only one prediction, which matches the only one ground truth annotation in ground_truths. For false positive, there is one and only one prediction, which doesn't match any ground truth annotation of the corresponding data_item_view_id. For false negative, there are zero or more predictions which are similar to the only ground truth annotation in ground_truths but not enough for a match. The schema of the prediction is stored in ModelEvaluation.annotation_schema_uri
---@field groundTruths? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentList Output only. The ground truth Annotations, i.e. the Annotations that exist in the test data the Model is evaluated on. For true positive, there is one and only one ground truth annotation, which matches the only prediction in predictions. For false positive, there are zero or more ground truth annotations that are similar to the only prediction in predictions, but not enough for a match. For false negative, there is one and only one ground truth annotation, which doesn't match any predictions created by the model. The schema of the ground truth is stored in ModelEvaluation.annotation_schema_uri
---@field type? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluatedAnnotationTypeEnum|string Output only. Type of the EvaluatedAnnotation.
---@field dataItemPayload? any Output only. The data item payload that the Model predicted this EvaluatedAnnotation on.
---@field evaluatedDataItemViewId? string Output only. ID of the EvaluatedDataItemView under the same ancestor ModelEvaluation. The EvaluatedDataItemView consists of all ground truths and predictions on data_item_payload.

---Explanation result of the prediction produced by the Model.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluatedAnnotationExplanation
---@field explanation? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Explanation Explanation attribution response details.
---@field explanationType? string Explanation type. For AutoML Image Classification models, possible values are: * `image-integrated-gradients` * `image-xrai`

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluatedAnnotationExplanationList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluatedAnnotationExplanation[]

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluatedAnnotationList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluatedAnnotation[]

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluatedAnnotationTypeEnum "EVALUATED_ANNOTATION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"TRUE_POSITIVE"|"FALSE_POSITIVE"|"FALSE_NEGATIVE"

---Evaluation Config for Tuning Job.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationConfig
---@field datasetCustomMetrics? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1DatasetCustomMetricList Optional. Specifications for custom dataset-level aggregations.
---@field inferenceGenerationConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GenerationConfig Optional. Configuration options for inference generation and outputs. If not set, default generation parameters are used.
---@field metrics? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1MetricList Required. The metrics used for evaluation.
---@field outputConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OutputConfig Required. Config for evaluation output.
---@field autoraterConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AutoraterConfig Optional. Autorater config for evaluation.

---The dataset used for evaluation.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationDataset
---@field bigquerySource? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1BigQuerySource BigQuery source holds the dataset.
---@field gcsSource? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GcsSource Cloud storage source holds the dataset. Currently only one Cloud Storage file path is supported.

---A single instance to be evaluated. Instances are used to specify the input data for evaluation, from simple string comparisons to complex, multi-turn model evaluations
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationInstance
---@field interactionsDataSource? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationInstanceInteractionsDataSource Optional. Source for populating `AgentData` from an Interactions API interaction. If set, no other agent data source fields (`cloud_trace_agent_data_source`, `agent_eval_data`, `agent_data`) may be set. The request will be rejected with INVALID_ARGUMENT if multiple agent data sources are provided.
---@field prompt? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationInstanceInstanceData Optional. Data used to populate placeholder `prompt` in a metric prompt template.
---@field response? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationInstanceInstanceData Optional. Data used to populate placeholder `response` in a metric prompt template.
---@field agentData? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationInstanceDeprecatedAgentData Optional. Deprecated: Use `agent_eval_data` instead. Data used for agent evaluation.
---@field agentEvalData? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentData Optional. Data used for agent evaluation.
---@field rubricGroups? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RubricGroupMap Optional. Named groups of rubrics associated with the prompt. This is used for rubric-based evaluations where rubrics can be referenced by a key. The key could represent versions, associated metrics, etc.
---@field otherData? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationInstanceMapInstance Optional. Other data used to populate placeholders based on their key. If a key conflicts with a field in the EvaluationInstance (e.g. `prompt`), the value of the field will take precedence over the value in other_data.
---@field reference? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationInstanceInstanceData Optional. Data used to populate placeholder `reference` in a metric prompt template.

---Deprecated: Use `google.cloud.aiplatform.master.AgentConfig` in `agent_eval_data` instead. Configuration for an Agent.
