---EvaluationItem is a single evaluation request or result. The content of an EvaluationItem is immutable - it cannot be updated once created. EvaluationItems can be deleted when no longer needed.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationItem
---@field evaluationResponse? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationResult Output only. The response from evaluation.
---@field evaluationItemType? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationItemEvaluationItemTypeEnum Required. The type of the EvaluationItem.
---@field gcsUri? string The Cloud Storage object where the request or response is stored.
---@field error? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Error for the evaluation item.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the EvaluationItem. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationItems/{evaluation_item}`
---@field metadata? any Optional. Metadata for the EvaluationItem.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the EvaluationItem.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap Optional. Labels for the EvaluationItem.
---@field evaluationRequest? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRequest The request to evaluate.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this item was created.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationItemEvaluationItemTypeEnum "EVALUATION_ITEM_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"REQUEST"|"RESULT"

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationItemList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationItem[]

---EvaluationMetric is a resource that represents a reusable metric configuration.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationMetric
---@field gcsUri? string Optional. The Google Cloud Storage URI that stores the metric specification..
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time when the EvaluationMetric was last updated.
---@field displayName? string Required. The user-friendly display name for the EvaluationMetric.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time when the EvaluationMetric was created.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap Optional. Labels for the evaluation metric.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the EvaluationMetric. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationMetrics/{evaluation_metric}`
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Optional. Customer-managed encryption key spec for this EvaluationMetric. If set, this EvaluationMetric will be secured by this key.
---@field metric? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Metric Optional. The metric configuration. Only LLMMetric and CustomCodeExecutionMetric are supported.
---@field description? string Optional. A description of the EvaluationMetric.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationMetricList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationMetric[]

---Config for parsing LLM responses. It can be used to parse the LLM response to be evaluated, or the LLM response from LLM-based metrics/Autoraters.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationParserConfig
---@field customCodeParserConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationParserConfigCustomCodeParserConfig Optional. Use custom code to parse the LLM response.

---Configuration for parsing the LLM response using custom code.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationParserConfigCustomCodeParserConfig
---@field parsingFunction? string Required. Python function for parsing results. The function should be defined within this string. The function takes a list of strings (LLM responses) and should return either a list of dictionaries (for rubrics) or a single dictionary (for a metric result). Example function signature: def parse(responses: list[str]) -> list[dict[str, Any]] | dict[str, Any]: When parsing rubrics, return a list of dictionaries, where each dictionary represents a Rubric. Example for rubrics: [ { "content": {"property": {"description": "The response is factual."}}, "type": "FACTUALITY", "importance": "HIGH" }, { "content": {"property": {"description": "The response is fluent."}}, "type": "FLUENCY", "importance": "MEDIUM" } ] When parsing critique results, return a dictionary representing a MetricResult. Example for a metric result: { "score": 0.8, "explanation": "The model followed most instructions.", "rubric_verdicts": [...] } ... code for result extraction and aggregation

---Prompt to be evaluated. This can represent a single-turn prompt or a multi-turn conversation for agent evaluations.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationPrompt
---@field text? string Text prompt.
---@field userScenario? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationPromptUserScenario Optional. The generated user scenario used to drive multi-turn agent running results.
---@field agentData? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentData Optional. Represents the complete execution trace of a multi-turn conversation, which can involve single or multiple agents. This serves as the input context for agent scraping.
---@field promptTemplateData? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationPromptPromptTemplateData Prompt template data.
---@field value? any Fields and values that can be used to populate the prompt template.

---Message to hold a prompt template and the values to populate the template.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationPromptPromptTemplateData
---@field values? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ContentMap_ The values for fields in the prompt template.

---User scenario to help simulate multi-turn agent running results.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationPromptUserScenario
---@field startingPrompt? string Required. The prompt that starts the conversation between the simulated user and the agent under test.
---@field conversationPlan? string Required. The plan for the conversation, used to drive the multi-turn agent run and generate the simulated agent evaluation dataset.

---A single evaluation request supporting input for both single-turn model generation and multi-turn agent execution traces. Valid input modes: 1. Inference Mode: `prompt` is set (containing text or AgentData context). 2. Offline Eval Mode: `prompt` is unset, and `candidate_responses` contains `agent_data` (the completed execution trace). Validation Rule: Either `prompt` must be set, OR at least one of the `candidate_responses` must contain `agent_data`. Metrics receive each candidate as an `EvaluationInstance`, whose fields are the names metrics can reference: `prompt` -> `prompt`, the candidate -> `response` (or `agent_eval_data` for `agent_data`), `golden_response` -> `reference`, `rubrics` -> `rubric_groups`, and `prompt.prompt_template_data.values` and `extra_context` -> `other_data`.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRequest
---@field rubrics? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RubricGroupMap Optional. Named groups of rubrics associated with this prompt. The key is a user-defined name for the rubric group.
---@field prompt? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationPrompt Optional. The request/prompt to evaluate.
---@field goldenResponse? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1CandidateResponse Optional. The Ideal response or ground truth.
---@field candidateResponses? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1CandidateResponseList Optional. Responses from model under test and other baseline models for comparison.

---Evaluation result.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationResult
---@field evaluationRun? string Required. The evaluation run that was used to generate the result. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationRuns/{evaluation_run}
---@field metadata? any Optional. Metadata about the evaluation result.
---@field request? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRequest Required. The request that was evaluated.
---@field evaluationRequest? string Required. The request item that was evaluated. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationItems/{evaluation_item}
---@field metric? string Required. The metric that was evaluated.
---@field candidateResults? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1CandidateResultList Optional. The results for the metric.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationResultList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationResult[]

---The results of the evaluation run.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationResults
---@field summaryMetrics? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1SummaryMetrics Optional. The summary metrics for the evaluation run.
---@field evaluationSet? string The evaluation set where item level results are stored.

---Configuration for a rubric group to be generated/saved for evaluation.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRubricConfig
---@field rubricGroupKey? string Required. The key used to save the generated rubrics. If a generation spec is provided, this key will be used for the name of the generated rubric group. Otherwise, this key will be used to look up the existing rubric group on the evaluation item. Note that if a rubric group key is specified on both a rubric config and an evaluation metric, the key from the metric will be used to select the rubrics for evaluation.
---@field rubricGenerationSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunMetricRubricGenerationSpec Dynamically generate rubrics using this specification.
---@field predefinedRubricGenerationSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunMetricPredefinedMetricSpec Dynamically generate rubrics using a predefined spec.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRubricConfigList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRubricConfig[]

---EvaluationRun is a resource that represents a single evaluation run, which includes a set of prompts, model responses, evaluation configuration and the resulting metrics.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRun
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the Evaluation Run.
---@field evaluationConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfig Optional. The configuration used for the evaluation. Optional when analysis_configs is provided.
---@field evaluationResults? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationResults Output only. The results of the evaluation run. Only populated when the evaluation run's state is SUCCEEDED.
---@field error? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Only populated when the evaluation run's state is FAILED or CANCELLED.
---@field dataSource? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunDataSource Required. The data source for the evaluation run.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Optional. Customer-managed encryption key spec for this EvaluationRun. If set, this EvaluationRun will be secured by this key.
---@field completionTime? string Output only. Time when the evaluation run was completed.
---@field metadata? any Optional. Metadata about the evaluation run, can be used by the caller to store additional tracking information about the evaluation run.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the EvaluationRun. This is a unique identifier. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationRuns/{evaluation_run}`
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunStateEnum Output only. The state of the evaluation run.
---@field inferenceConfigs? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigMap Optional. The candidate to inference config map for the evaluation run. The candidate can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when the evaluation run was created.
---@field serviceAccount? string Optional. The service account to run the evaluation run as. If set, the run uses this service account to access Google Cloud resources. Access is limited to the IAM permissions that you grant to the service account. Must be provided if an inference config sets `harbor_run_config`, `data_agent_config`. If no inference config requires this field, setting it returns an error. The caller must have the `iam.serviceAccounts.actAs` permission on this service account, and the project's [Vertex AI Service Agent](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/general/access-control#service-agents) must have the `roles/iam.serviceAccountTokenCreator` role on it.
---@field evaluationSetSnapshot? string Output only. The specific evaluation set of the evaluation run. For runs with an evaluation set input, this will be that same set. For runs with BigQuery input, it's the sampled BigQuery dataset.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap Optional. Labels for the evaluation run.

---The data source for the evaluation run.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunDataSource
---@field bigqueryRequestSet? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1BigQueryRequestSet Evaluation data in bigquery.
---@field evaluationSet? string The EvaluationSet resource name. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationSets/{evaluation_set}`

---The Evalution configuration used for the evaluation run.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfig
---@field metrics? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunMetricList Optional. The metrics to be calculated in the evaluation run. Required when analysis_configs is not set.
---@field allowCrossRegionModel? boolean Optional. Allows the evaluation run to use cross region models. When this flag is set, the service may route traffic to other regions if a model is unavailable in the current region (e.g., to a `global` endpoint). If a fully-qualified model endpoint resource name with a different region than the run location is provided elsewhere in the run config, this flag must be set to true or the request will fail.
---@field lossAnalysisConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1LossAnalysisConfigList Optional. Specifications for loss analysis. Each config can be specified for one metric.
---@field datasetCustomMetrics? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1DatasetCustomMetricList Optional. Specifications for custom dataset-level aggregations.
---@field promptTemplate? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigPromptTemplate The prompt template used for inference. The values for variables in the prompt template are defined in EvaluationItem.EvaluationPrompt.PromptTemplateData.values.
---@field rubricConfigs? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRubricConfigList Optional. The rubric configs for the evaluation run. They are used to generate rubrics which can be used by rubric-based metrics. Multiple rubric configs can be specified for rubric generation but only one rubric config can be used for a rubric-based metric. If more than one rubric config is provided, the evaluation metric must specify a rubric group key. Note that if a generation spec is specified on both a rubric config and an evaluation metric, the rubrics generated for the metric will be used for evaluation.
---@field cloudLoggingConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1CloudLoggingConfig Optional. Configuration for exporting evaluation results to Cloud Logging.
---@field autoraterConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigAutoraterConfig Optional. The autorater config for the evaluation run.
---@field outputConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigOutputConfig Optional. The output config for the evaluation run.

---The autorater config used for the evaluation run.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigAutoraterConfig
---@field generationConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GenerationConfig Optional. Configuration options for model generation and outputs.
---@field autoraterModel? string Optional. The fully qualified name of the publisher model or tuned autorater endpoint to use. Publisher model format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/*/models/*` Tuned model endpoint format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/endpoints/{endpoint}`
---@field sampleCount? number Optional. Number of samples for each instance in the dataset. If not specified, the default is 4. Minimum value is 1, maximum value is 32.

---The output config for the evaluation run.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigOutputConfig
---@field bigqueryDestination? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1BigQueryDestination BigQuery destination for evaluation output.
---@field gcsDestination? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GcsDestination Cloud Storage destination for evaluation output.

---Prompt template used for inference.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigPromptTemplate
---@field gcsUri? string Prompt template stored in Cloud Storage. Format: "gs://my-bucket/file-name.txt".
---@field promptTemplate? string Inline prompt template. Template variables should be in the format "{var_name}". Example: "Translate the following from {source_lang} to {target_lang}: {text}"

---Defines the configuration for a candidate model or agent being evaluated. `InferenceConfig` encapsulates all the necessary information to invoke or scrape the candidate during the evaluation run. This includes direct model inference parameters, agent execution settings, and multi-turn scraping configurations (such as user simulators). It serves as the primary representation of the candidate across different stages of the evaluation process.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunInferenceConfig
---@field agentRunConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigAgentRunConfig Optional. Agent run config.
---@field promptTemplate? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigPromptTemplate Optional. The prompt template used for inference. The values for variables in the prompt template are defined in EvaluationItem.EvaluationPrompt.PromptTemplateData.values. If not specified, the prompt template in the EvaluationConfig will be used.
---@field model? string Optional. The fully qualified name of the publisher model or endpoint to use. Anthropic and Llama third-party models are also supported through Model Garden. Publisher model format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/*/models/*` Third-party model formats: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/anthropic/models/{model}` or `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/llama/models/{model}` Endpoint format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/endpoints/{endpoint}`
---@field parallelism? number Optional. The parallelism of the evaluation run for the inference step. If not specified, the default parallelism will be used.
---@field generationConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GenerationConfig Optional. Generation config.
---@field agents? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentConfigMap Optional. Contains the static configurations for each agent in the system. Key: agent_id (matches the `author` field in events). Value: The static configuration of the agent.

---Configuration for Agent Run.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigAgentRunConfig
---@field sessionInput? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigSessionInput Optional. The session input to get agent running results.
---@field userSimulatorConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigAgentRunConfigUserSimulatorConfig The configuration for a user simulator that uses an LLM to generate messages on behalf of the user.
---@field geminiAgentConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GeminiAgentConfig Optional. Config for scraping a Gemini Agent via the Interactions API. The scraping service creates interactions against the agent and returns the resulting interaction traces for evaluation.
---@field agentEngine? string Optional. The resource name of the Agent Engine. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine} For example: projects/123/locations/us-central1/reasoningEngines/456
---@field dataAgentConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1DataAgentConfig Optional. Config for scraping a Gemini Data Analytics data agent. The scraping service runs the agent via the DataChatService Chat API and returns the resulting trajectory for evaluation.

---Used for multi-turn agent scraping. Contains configuration for a user simulator that uses an LLM to generate messages on behalf of the user.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigAgentRunConfigUserSimulatorConfig
---@field modelName? string The model name to use for multi-turn agent scraping to get next user message, e.g. "gemini-3-flash-preview".
---@field modelConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GenerationConfig The configuration for the model.
---@field maxTurn? number Maximum number of invocations allowed by the multi-turn agent scraping. This property allows us to stop a run-off conversation, where the agent and the user simulator get into a never ending loop. The initial fixed prompt is also counted as an invocation.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigMap { [string]: gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunInferenceConfig }

---Session input to run an Agent.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigSessionInput
---@field parameters? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap Optional. Additional parameters for the session, like app_name, etc. For example, {"app_name": "my-app"}.
---@field userId? string Optional. The user id for the agent session. The ID can be up to 128 characters long.
---@field sessionState? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentMap Optional. Session specific memory which stores key conversation points.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRun[]

---The metric used for evaluation runs.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunMetric
---@field metricResourceName? string Optional. The resource name of the metric definition.
---@field computationBasedMetricSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunMetricComputationBasedMetricSpec Spec for a computation based metric.
---@field metric? string Required. The name of the metric.
---@field metricConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Metric The metric config.
---@field predefinedMetricSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunMetricPredefinedMetricSpec Spec for a pre-defined metric.
