---A predicted FunctionCall returned from the model that contains a string representing the FunctionDeclaration.name and a structured JSON object containing the parameters and their values.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FunctionCall
---@field id? string Optional. The unique id of the function call. If populated, the client to execute the `function_call` and return the response with the matching `id`.
---@field willContinue? boolean Optional. Whether this is the last part of the FunctionCall. If true, another partial message for the current FunctionCall is expected to follow.
---@field name? string Optional. The name of the function to call. Matches FunctionDeclaration.name.
---@field args? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentMap Optional. The function parameters and values in JSON object format. See FunctionDeclaration.parameters for parameter details.
---@field partialArgs? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PartialArgList Optional. The partial argument value of the function call. If provided, represents the arguments/fields that are streamed incrementally.

---Function calling config.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FunctionCallingConfig
---@field mode? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FunctionCallingConfigModeEnum|string Optional. Function calling mode.
---@field streamFunctionCallArguments? boolean Optional. When set to true, arguments of a single function call will be streamed out in multiple parts/contents/responses. Partial parameter results will be returned in the `FunctionCall.partial_args` field.
---@field allowedFunctionNames? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. Function names to call. Only set when the Mode is ANY. Function names should match FunctionDeclaration.name. With mode set to ANY, model will predict a function call from the set of function names provided.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FunctionCallingConfigModeEnum "MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"AUTO"|"ANY"|"NONE"|"VALIDATED"

---Structured representation of a function declaration as defined by the [OpenAPI 3.0 specification](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.0.3). Included in this declaration are the function name, description, parameters and response type. This FunctionDeclaration is a representation of a block of code that can be used as a `Tool` by the model and executed by the client.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FunctionDeclaration
---@field responseJsonSchema? any Optional. Describes the output from this function in JSON Schema format. The value specified by the schema is the response value of the function. This field is mutually exclusive with `response`.
---@field name? string Required. The name of the function to call. Must start with a letter or an underscore. Must be a-z, A-Z, 0-9, or contain underscores, dots, colons and dashes, with a maximum length of 128.
---@field description? string Optional. Description and purpose of the function. Model uses it to decide how and whether to call the function.
---@field behavior? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FunctionDeclarationBehaviorEnum|string Optional. Specifies the function Behavior. If not specified, the system keeps the current function call behavior. This field is currently only supported by the BidiGenerateContent method.
---@field response? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Schema Optional. Describes the output from this function in JSON Schema format. Reflects the Open API 3.03 Response Object. The Schema defines the type used for the response value of the function.
---@field parametersJsonSchema? any Optional. Describes the parameters to the function in JSON Schema format. The schema must describe an object where the properties are the parameters to the function. For example: ``` { "type": "object", "properties": { "name": { "type": "string" }, "age": { "type": "integer" } }, "additionalProperties": false, "required": ["name", "age"], "propertyOrdering": ["name", "age"] } ``` This field is mutually exclusive with `parameters`.
---@field parameters? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Schema Optional. Describes the parameters to this function in JSON Schema Object format. Reflects the Open API 3.03 Parameter Object. string Key: the name of the parameter. Parameter names are case sensitive. Schema Value: the Schema defining the type used for the parameter. For function with no parameters, this can be left unset. Parameter names must start with a letter or an underscore and must only contain chars a-z, A-Z, 0-9, or underscores with a maximum length of 64. Example with 1 required and 1 optional parameter: type: OBJECT properties: param1: type: STRING param2: type: INTEGER required: - param1

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FunctionDeclarationBehaviorEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"BLOCKING"|"NON_BLOCKING"

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FunctionDeclarationList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FunctionDeclaration[]

---The result output from a FunctionCall that contains a string representing the FunctionDeclaration.name and a structured JSON object containing any output from the function is used as context to the model. This should contain the result of a `FunctionCall` made based on model prediction.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FunctionResponse
---@field scheduling? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FunctionResponseSchedulingEnum|string Optional. Specifies how the response should be scheduled in the conversation. Only applicable to NON_BLOCKING function calls, is ignored otherwise. Defaults to WHEN_IDLE.
---@field response? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentMap Required. The function response in JSON object format. Use "output" key to specify function output and "error" key to specify error details (if any). If "output" and "error" keys are not specified, then whole "response" is treated as function output.
---@field name? string Required. The name of the function to call. Matches FunctionDeclaration.name and FunctionCall.name.
---@field id? string Optional. The id of the function call this response is for. Populated by the client to match the corresponding function call `id`.
---@field parts? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FunctionResponsePartList Optional. Ordered `Parts` that constitute a function response. Parts may have different IANA MIME types.

---Raw media bytes for function response. Text should not be sent as raw bytes, use the 'text' field.
