---@field title? string The title of the web page that contains the evidence.

---Information about the sources that support the content of a response. When grounding is enabled, the model returns citations for claims in the response. This object contains the retrieved sources.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GroundingMetadata
---@field googleMapsWidgetContextToken? string Optional. Output only. Deprecated: The Google Maps contextual widget behavior in Grounding with Google Maps is being deprecated; this field is planned for removal and will no longer be populated once removed. A token that can be used to render a Google Maps widget with the contextual data. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Maps.
---@field groundingChunks? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GroundingChunkList A list of supporting references retrieved from the grounding source. This field is populated when the grounding source is Google Search, Vertex AI Search, or Google Maps.
---@field searchEntryPoint? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1SearchEntryPoint Optional. A web search entry point that can be used to display search results. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Search.
---@field retrievalMetadata? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RetrievalMetadata Optional. Output only. Metadata related to the retrieval grounding source.
---@field sourceFlaggingUris? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GroundingMetadataSourceFlaggingUriList Optional. Output only. A list of URIs that can be used to flag a place or review for inappropriate content. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Maps.
---@field retrievalQueries? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. The queries that were executed by the retrieval tools. This field is populated only when the grounding source is a retrieval tool, such as Vertex AI Search.
---@field imageSearchQueries? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. The image search queries that were used to generate the content. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Search with the Image Search search_type enabled.
---@field webSearchQueries? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. The web search queries that were used to generate the content. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Search.
---@field groundingSupports? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GroundingSupportList Optional. A list of grounding supports that connect the generated content to the grounding chunks. This field is populated when the grounding source is Google Search or Vertex AI Search.

---A URI that can be used to flag a place or review for inappropriate content. This is populated only when the grounding source is Google Maps.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GroundingMetadataSourceFlaggingUri
---@field sourceId? string The ID of the place or review.
---@field flagContentUri? string The URI that can be used to flag the content.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GroundingMetadataSourceFlaggingUriList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GroundingMetadataSourceFlaggingUri[]

---A collection of supporting references for a segment or part of the model's response.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GroundingSupport
---@field segment? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Segment The content segment that this support message applies to.
---@field renderedParts? gcp.aiplatform_v1.IntegerList Indices into the `rendered_parts` field of the `GroundingMetadata` message. These indices specify which rendered parts are associated with this support message.
---@field groundingChunkIndices? gcp.aiplatform_v1.IntegerList A list of indices into the `grounding_chunks` field of the `GroundingMetadata` message. These indices specify which grounding chunks support the claim made in the content segment. For example, if this field has the values `[1, 3]`, it means that `grounding_chunks[1]` and `grounding_chunks[3]` are the sources for the claim in the content segment.
---@field confidenceScores? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DoubleList The confidence scores for the support references. This list is parallel to the `grounding_chunk_indices` list. A score is a value between 0.0 and 1.0, with a higher score indicating a higher confidence that the reference supports the claim. For Gemini 2.0 and before, this list has the same size as `grounding_chunk_indices`. For Gemini 2.5 and later, this list is empty and should be ignored.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GroundingSupportList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GroundingSupport[]

---Represents a HyperparameterTuningJob. A HyperparameterTuningJob has a Study specification and multiple CustomJobs with identical CustomJob specification.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1HyperparameterTuningJob
---@field endTime? string Output only. Time when the HyperparameterTuningJob entered any of the following states: `JOB_STATE_SUCCEEDED`, `JOB_STATE_FAILED`, `JOB_STATE_CANCELLED`.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the HyperparameterTuningJob. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field studySpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1StudySpec Required. Study configuration of the HyperparameterTuningJob.
---@field trialJobSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1CustomJobSpec Required. The spec of a trial job. The same spec applies to the CustomJobs created in all the trials.
---@field maxFailedTrialCount? number The number of failed Trials that need to be seen before failing the HyperparameterTuningJob. If set to 0, Vertex AI decides how many Trials must fail before the whole job fails.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the HyperparameterTuningJob.
---@field error? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Only populated when job's state is JOB_STATE_FAILED or JOB_STATE_CANCELLED.
---@field trials? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1TrialList Output only. Trials of the HyperparameterTuningJob.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize HyperparameterTuningJobs. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time when the HyperparameterTuningJob was most recently updated.
---@field parallelTrialCount? number Required. The desired number of Trials to run in parallel.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1HyperparameterTuningJobStateEnum Output only. The detailed state of the job.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when the HyperparameterTuningJob was created.
---@field maxTrialCount? number Required. The desired total number of Trials.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Time when the HyperparameterTuningJob for the first time entered the `JOB_STATE_RUNNING` state.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key options for a HyperparameterTuningJob. If this is set, then all resources created by the HyperparameterTuningJob will be encrypted with the provided encryption key.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1HyperparameterTuningJobList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1HyperparameterTuningJob[]

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1HyperparameterTuningJobStateEnum "JOB_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"JOB_STATE_QUEUED"|"JOB_STATE_PENDING"|"JOB_STATE_RUNNING"|"JOB_STATE_SUCCEEDED"|"JOB_STATE_FAILED"|"JOB_STATE_CANCELLING"|"JOB_STATE_CANCELLED"|"JOB_STATE_PAUSED"|"JOB_STATE_EXPIRED"|"JOB_STATE_UPDATING"|"JOB_STATE_PARTIALLY_SUCCEEDED"

---Matcher for Features of an EntityType by Feature ID.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IdMatcher
---@field ids? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Required. The following are accepted as `ids`: * A single-element list containing only `*`, which selects all Features in the target EntityType, or * A list containing only Feature IDs, which selects only Features with those IDs in the target EntityType.

---Configuration for image generation. This message allows you to control various aspects of image generation, such as the output format, aspect ratio, and whether the model can generate images of people.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageConfig
---@field personGeneration? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageConfigPersonGenerationEnum|string Optional. Controls whether the model can generate people.
---@field imageOutputOptions? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageConfigImageOutputOptions Optional. The image output format for generated images.
---@field imageSize? string Optional. Specifies the size of generated images. Supported values are `1K`, `2K`, `4K`. If not specified, the model will use default value `1K`.
---@field prominentPeople? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageConfigProminentPeopleEnum|string Optional. Controls whether prominent people (celebrities) generation is allowed. If used with personGeneration, personGeneration enum would take precedence. For instance, if ALLOW_NONE is set, all person generation would be blocked. If this field is unspecified, the default behavior is to allow prominent people.
---@field aspectRatio? string Optional. The desired aspect ratio for the generated images. The following aspect ratios are supported: "1:1" "2:3", "3:2" "3:4", "4:3" "4:5", "5:4" "9:16", "16:9" "21:9"

---The image output format for generated images.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageConfigImageOutputOptions
---@field compressionQuality? number Optional. The compression quality of the output image.
---@field mimeType? string Optional. The image format that the output should be saved as.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageConfigPersonGenerationEnum "PERSON_GENERATION_UNSPECIFIED"|"ALLOW_ALL"|"ALLOW_ADULT"|"ALLOW_NONE"

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageConfigProminentPeopleEnum "PROMINENT_PEOPLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ALLOW_PROMINENT_PEOPLE"|"BLOCK_PROMINENT_PEOPLE"

---Configuration for image-specific output formatting.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageResponseFormat
---@field imageSize? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageResponseFormatImageSizeEnum|string Optional. The size of the image output.
---@field delivery? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageResponseFormatDeliveryEnum|string Optional. Delivery mode for the generated content.
---@field aspectRatio? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageResponseFormatAspectRatioEnum|string Optional. The aspect ratio for the image output.
---@field mimeType? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageResponseFormatMimeTypeEnum|string Optional. The MIME type of the image output.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageResponseFormatAspectRatioEnum "ASPECT_RATIO_UNSPECIFIED"|"ASPECT_RATIO_ONE_BY_ONE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_TWO_BY_THREE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_THREE_BY_TWO"|"ASPECT_RATIO_THREE_BY_FOUR"|"ASPECT_RATIO_FOUR_BY_THREE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_FOUR_BY_FIVE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_FIVE_BY_FOUR"|"ASPECT_RATIO_NINE_BY_SIXTEEN"|"ASPECT_RATIO_SIXTEEN_BY_NINE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_TWENTY_ONE_BY_NINE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_ONE_BY_EIGHT"|"ASPECT_RATIO_EIGHT_BY_ONE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_ONE_BY_FOUR"|"ASPECT_RATIO_FOUR_BY_ONE"

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageResponseFormatDeliveryEnum "DELIVERY_UNSPECIFIED"|"INLINE"|"URI"

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageResponseFormatImageSizeEnum "IMAGE_SIZE_UNSPECIFIED"|"IMAGE_SIZE_FIVE_TWELVE"|"IMAGE_SIZE_ONE_K"|"IMAGE_SIZE_TWO_K"|"IMAGE_SIZE_FOUR_K"

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImageResponseFormatMimeTypeEnum "MIME_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"IMAGE_JPEG"

---Describes the location from where we import data into a Dataset, together with the labels that will be applied to the DataItems and the Annotations.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportDataConfig
---@field dataItemLabels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap Labels that will be applied to newly imported DataItems. If an identical DataItem as one being imported already exists in the Dataset, then these labels will be appended to these of the already existing one, and if labels with identical key is imported before, the old label value will be overwritten. If two DataItems are identical in the same import data operation, the labels will be combined and if key collision happens in this case, one of the values will be picked randomly. Two DataItems are considered identical if their content bytes are identical (e.g. image bytes or pdf bytes). These labels will be overridden by Annotation labels specified inside index file referenced by import_schema_uri, e.g. jsonl file.
---@field gcsSource? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GcsSource The Google Cloud Storage location for the input content.
---@field annotationLabels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap Labels that will be applied to newly imported Annotations. If two Annotations are identical, one of them will be deduped. Two Annotations are considered identical if their payload, payload_schema_uri and all of their labels are the same. These labels will be overridden by Annotation labels specified inside index file referenced by import_schema_uri, e.g. jsonl file.
---@field importSchemaUri? string Required. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing the import format. Validation will be done against the schema. The schema is defined as an [OpenAPI 3.0.2 Schema Object](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.0.2.md#schemaObject).

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportDataConfigList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportDataConfig[]

---Source for loading Agent Engine sessions.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportEvaluationSetRequestAgentEngineSource
---@field location? string Required. Location for the Agent Engine sessions.
---@field sessionIds? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Required. Session IDs for the Agent Engine sessions to retrieve.
---@field reasoningEngineId? string Required. Reasoning Engine ID for the Agent Engine sessions.
---@field projectId? string Required. Project ID for the Agent Engine sessions.

---Source for loading traces directly from Cloud Trace.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportEvaluationSetRequestCloudTraceSource
---@field agentResource? string Optional. Restricts the imported spans to a single agent. Accepts either of two forms, matching `OnlineEvaluator.agent_resource`: * a project-scoped resource name, matched against the `cloud.resource_id` resource attribute that Vertex AI Agent Engine agents are stamped with; * an Agent Registry agent URN, matched against the `gen_ai.main_agent.id` resource attribute that agents on GKE, and any other runtime that stamps it, are identified by. Scopes `session_ids` selection only. Traces named explicitly in `trace_ids` are imported as given and are NOT filtered by this field, because the caller has already identified them. Setting this field with only `trace_ids` therefore has no effect. When unset, spans are selected by session or trace ID alone. That is the pre-existing behavior and it remains the correct one for a session whose agents run in several deployments, because each deployment stamps its own `gen_ai.main_agent.id` and filtering on one of them would silently truncate the trajectory.
---@field sessionIds? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. Session IDs to import traces for. If both trace_ids and session_ids are specified, the union of the two will be imported.
---@field projectId? string Required. Project ID for the Cloud Trace.
---@field traceIds? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. Trace IDs to import.

---Source for loading data from Cloud Storage.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportEvaluationSetRequestGcsSource
---@field importSchemaConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportEvaluationSetRequestImportSchemaConfig Required. Schema configuration for the input data.
---@field gcsUri? string Required. The Cloud Storage location of the input data.

---Configuration for the input data format.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportEvaluationSetRequestImportSchemaConfig
---@field dataFormat? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportEvaluationSetRequestImportSchemaConfigDataFormatEnum|string Required. The format of the input data.
---@field dataFormatVersion? string Optional. Version of the data format.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportEvaluationSetRequestImportSchemaConfigDataFormatEnum "DATA_FORMAT_UNSPECIFIED"|"OTEL_PROTO"|"OTEL_JSON"|"JSONL"

---Wrapper for inline data.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportEvaluationSetRequestInlineSource
---@field importSchemaConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportEvaluationSetRequestImportSchemaConfig Required. Schema configuration for the inline data.
---@field content? string Required. The content of the inline data.

---Source for importing interactions from the Interactions API into an EvaluationSet. The agent identity is specified once, with a list of interaction IDs to import.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportEvaluationSetRequestInteractionsSource
---@field interactions? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Required. The interactions to import. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/interactions/{interaction}`.
---@field geminiAgentConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GeminiAgentConfig Optional. Gemini Agent (Vertex AI Agent resource).

---Defines the Feature value(s) to import.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportFeatureValuesRequestFeatureSpec
---@field id? string Required. ID of the Feature to import values of. This Feature must exist in the target EntityType, or the request will fail.
---@field sourceField? string Source column to get the Feature values from. If not set, uses the column with the same name as the Feature ID.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportFeatureValuesRequestFeatureSpecList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportFeatureValuesRequestFeatureSpec[]

---Config for importing RagFiles.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ImportRagFilesConfig
---@field sharePointSources? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1SharePointSources SharePoint sources.
---@field jiraSource? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1JiraSource Jira queries with their corresponding authentication.
---@field slackSource? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1SlackSource Slack channels with their corresponding access tokens.
---@field maxEmbeddingRequestsPerMin? number Optional. The max number of queries per minute that this job is allowed to make to the embedding model specified on the corpus. This value is specific to this job and not shared across other import jobs. Consult the Quotas page on the project to set an appropriate value here. If unspecified, a default value of 1,000 QPM would be used.
---@field partialFailureBigquerySink? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1BigQueryDestination The BigQuery destination to write partial failures to. It should be a bigquery table resource name (e.g. "bq://projectId.bqDatasetId.bqTableId"). The dataset must exist. If the table does not exist, it will be created with the expected schema. If the table exists, the schema will be validated and data will be added to this existing table. Deprecated. Prefer to use `import_result_bq_sink`.
---@field rebuildAnnIndex? boolean Rebuilds the ANN index to optimize for recall on the imported data. Only applicable for RagCorpora running on RagManagedDb with `retrieval_strategy` set to `ANN`. The rebuild will be performed using the existing ANN config set on the RagCorpus. To change the ANN config, please use the UpdateRagCorpus API. Default is false, i.e., index is not rebuilt.
---@field gcsSource? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GcsSource Google Cloud Storage location. Supports importing individual files as well as entire Google Cloud Storage directories. Sample formats: - `gs://bucket_name/my_directory/object_name/my_file.txt` - `gs://bucket_name/my_directory`
---@field importResultGcsSink? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GcsDestination The Cloud Storage path to write import result to.
---@field ragFileTransformationConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagFileTransformationConfig Specifies the transformation config for RagFiles.
---@field partialFailureGcsSink? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GcsDestination The Cloud Storage path to write partial failures to. Deprecated. Prefer to use `import_result_gcs_sink`.
---@field importResultBigquerySink? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1BigQueryDestination The BigQuery destination to write import result to. It should be a bigquery table resource name (e.g. "bq://projectId.bqDatasetId.bqTableId"). The dataset must exist. If the table does not exist, it will be created with the expected schema. If the table exists, the schema will be validated and data will be added to this existing table.
---@field googleDriveSource? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GoogleDriveSource Google Drive location. Supports importing individual files as well as Google Drive folders.
---@field ragFileParsingConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagFileParsingConfig Optional. Specifies the parsing config for RagFiles. RAG will use the default parser if this field is not set.

---A representation of a collection of database items organized in a way that allows for approximate nearest neighbor (a.k.a ANN) algorithms search.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Index
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Index was created.
---@field metadata? any An additional information about the Index; the schema of the metadata can be found in metadata_schema.
---@field indexStats? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexStats Output only. Stats of the index resource.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Index was most recently updated. This also includes any update to the contents of the Index. Note that Operations working on this Index may have their Operations.metadata.generic_metadata.update_time a little after the value of this timestamp, yet that does not mean their results are not already reflected in the Index. Result of any successfully completed Operation on the Index is reflected in it.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the Index. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field etag? string Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Immutable. Customer-managed encryption key spec for an Index. If set, this Index and all sub-resources of this Index will be secured by this key.
---@field deployedIndexes? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1DeployedIndexRefList Output only. The pointers to DeployedIndexes created from this Index. An Index can be only deleted if all its DeployedIndexes had been undeployed first.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your Indexes. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field indexUpdateMethod? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexIndexUpdateMethodEnum Immutable. The update method to use with this Index. If not set, BATCH_UPDATE will be used by default.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the Index.
---@field description? string The description of the Index.
---@field metadataSchemaUri? string Immutable. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing additional information about the Index, that is specific to it. Unset if the Index does not have any additional information. The schema is defined as an OpenAPI 3.0.2 [Schema Object](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.0.2.md#schemaObject). Note: The URI given on output will be immutable and probably different, including the URI scheme, than the one given on input. The output URI will point to a location where the user only has a read access.

---A datapoint of Index.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapoint
---@field sparseEmbedding? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointSparseEmbedding Optional. Feature embedding vector for sparse index.
---@field numericRestricts? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointNumericRestrictionList Optional. List of Restrict of the datapoint, used to perform "restricted searches" where boolean rule are used to filter the subset of the database eligible for matching. This uses numeric comparisons.
---@field embeddingMetadata? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentMap Optional. The key-value map of additional metadata for the datapoint.
---@field featureVector? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DoubleList Required. Feature embedding vector for dense index. An array of numbers with the length of [NearestNeighborSearchConfig.dimensions].
---@field restricts? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointRestrictionList Optional. List of Restrict of the datapoint, used to perform "restricted searches" where boolean rule are used to filter the subset of the database eligible for matching. This uses categorical tokens. See: https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/matching-engine/filtering
---@field datapointId? string Required. Unique identifier of the datapoint.
---@field crowdingTag? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointCrowdingTag Optional. CrowdingTag of the datapoint, the number of neighbors to return in each crowding can be configured during query.

---Crowding tag is a constraint on a neighbor list produced by nearest neighbor search requiring that no more than some value k' of the k neighbors returned have the same value of crowding_attribute.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointCrowdingTag
---@field crowdingAttribute? string The attribute value used for crowding. The maximum number of neighbors to return per crowding attribute value (per_crowding_attribute_num_neighbors) is configured per-query. This field is ignored if per_crowding_attribute_num_neighbors is larger than the total number of neighbors to return for a given query.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapoint[]

---This field allows restricts to be based on numeric comparisons rather than categorical tokens.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointNumericRestriction
---@field valueDouble? number Represents 64 bit float.
---@field op? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointNumericRestrictionOpEnum|string This MUST be specified for queries and must NOT be specified for datapoints.
---@field valueFloat? number Represents 32 bit float.
---@field valueInt? string Represents 64 bit integer.
---@field namespace? string The namespace of this restriction. e.g.: cost.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointNumericRestrictionList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointNumericRestriction[]

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointNumericRestrictionOpEnum "OPERATOR_UNSPECIFIED"|"LESS"|"LESS_EQUAL"|"EQUAL"|"GREATER_EQUAL"|"GREATER"|"NOT_EQUAL"

---Restriction of a datapoint which describe its attributes(tokens) from each of several attribute categories(namespaces).
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointRestriction
---@field namespace? string The namespace of this restriction. e.g.: color.
---@field denyList? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList The attributes to deny in this namespace. e.g.: 'blue'
---@field allowList? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList The attributes to allow in this namespace. e.g.: 'red'

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointRestrictionList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointRestriction[]

---Feature embedding vector for sparse index. An array of numbers whose values are located in the specified dimensions.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexDatapointSparseEmbedding
---@field values? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DoubleList Required. The list of embedding values of the sparse vector.
---@field dimensions? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Required. The list of indexes for the embedding values of the sparse vector.

---Indexes are deployed into it. An IndexEndpoint can have multiple DeployedIndexes.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexEndpoint
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the IndexEndpoint.
---@field deployedIndexes? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1DeployedIndexList Output only. The indexes deployed in this endpoint.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field publicEndpointEnabled? boolean Optional. If true, the deployed index will be accessible through public endpoint.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your IndexEndpoints. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Immutable. Customer-managed encryption key spec for an IndexEndpoint. If set, this IndexEndpoint and all sub-resources of this IndexEndpoint will be secured by this key.
---@field description? string The description of the IndexEndpoint.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this IndexEndpoint was created.
---@field enablePrivateServiceConnect? boolean Optional. Deprecated: If true, expose the IndexEndpoint via private service connect. Only one of the fields, network or enable_private_service_connect, can be set.
---@field network? string Optional. The full name of the Google Compute Engine [network](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/networks-and-firewalls#networks) to which the IndexEndpoint should be peered. Private services access must already be configured for the network. If left unspecified, the Endpoint is not peered with any network. network and private_service_connect_config are mutually exclusive. [Format](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/reference/rest/v1/networks/insert): `projects/{project}/global/networks/{network}`. Where {project} is a project number, as in '12345', and {network} is network name.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the IndexEndpoint. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field etag? string Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this IndexEndpoint was last updated. This timestamp is not updated when the endpoint's DeployedIndexes are updated, e.g. due to updates of the original Indexes they are the deployments of.
---@field publicEndpointDomainName? string Output only. If public_endpoint_enabled is true, this field will be populated with the domain name to use for this index endpoint.
---@field privateServiceConnectConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PrivateServiceConnectConfig Optional. Configuration for private service connect. network and private_service_connect_config are mutually exclusive.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexEndpointList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexEndpoint[]

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexIndexUpdateMethodEnum "INDEX_UPDATE_METHOD_UNSPECIFIED"|"BATCH_UPDATE"|"STREAM_UPDATE"

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Index[]

---IndexPrivateEndpoints proto is used to provide paths for users to send requests via private endpoints (e.g. private service access, private service connect). To send request via private service access, use match_grpc_address. To send request via private service connect, use service_attachment.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexPrivateEndpoints
---@field serviceAttachment? string Output only. The name of the service attachment resource. Populated if private service connect is enabled.
---@field pscAutomatedEndpoints? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PscAutomatedEndpointsList Output only. PscAutomatedEndpoints is populated if private service connect is enabled if PscAutomatedConfig is set.
---@field matchGrpcAddress? string Output only. The ip address used to send match gRPC requests.

---Stats of the Index.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IndexStats
---@field vectorsCount? string Output only. The number of dense vectors in the Index.
---@field shardsCount? number Output only. The number of shards in the Index.
---@field sparseVectorsCount? string Output only. The number of sparse vectors in the Index.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IngestEventsRequestMetadataMergeStrategyEnum "METADATA_MERGE_STRATEGY_UNSPECIFIED"|"OVERWRITE"|"MERGE"|"REQUIRE_EXACT_MATCH"

---Ingest events directly from the request.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IngestionDirectContentsSource
---@field events? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IngestionDirectContentsSourceEventList Required. The events to ingest.

---A single event to ingest.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IngestionDirectContentsSourceEvent
---@field eventTime? string Optional. The time at which the event occurred. If provided, this timestamp will be used for ordering events within a stream. If not provided, the server-side ingestion time will be used.
---@field content? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Content Required. The content of the event.
---@field eventId? string Optional. A unique identifier for the event. If an event with the same event_id is ingested multiple times, it will be de-duplicated.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IngestionDirectContentsSourceEventList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IngestionDirectContentsSourceEvent[]

---Specifies Vertex AI owned input data to be used for training, and possibly evaluating, the Model.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1InputDataConfig
---@field bigqueryDestination? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1BigQueryDestination Only applicable to custom training with tabular Dataset with BigQuery source. The BigQuery project location where the training data is to be written to. In the given project a new dataset is created with name `dataset___` where timestamp is in YYYY_MM_DDThh_mm_ss_sssZ format. All training input data is written into that dataset. In the dataset three tables are created, `training`, `validation` and `test`. * AIP_DATA_FORMAT = "bigquery". * AIP_TRAINING_DATA_URI = "bigquery_destination.dataset___.training" * AIP_VALIDATION_DATA_URI = "bigquery_destination.dataset___.validation" * AIP_TEST_DATA_URI = "bigquery_destination.dataset___.test"
---@field savedQueryId? string Only applicable to Datasets that have SavedQueries. The ID of a SavedQuery (annotation set) under the Dataset specified by dataset_id used for filtering Annotations for training. Only Annotations that are associated with this SavedQuery are used in respectively training. When used in conjunction with annotations_filter, the Annotations used for training are filtered by both saved_query_id and annotations_filter. Only one of saved_query_id and annotation_schema_uri should be specified as both of them represent the same thing: problem type.
---@field stratifiedSplit? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1StratifiedSplit Supported only for tabular Datasets. Split based on the distribution of the specified column.
---@field timestampSplit? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1TimestampSplit Supported only for tabular Datasets. Split based on the timestamp of the input data pieces.
---@field predefinedSplit? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PredefinedSplit Supported only for tabular Datasets. Split based on a predefined key.
---@field fractionSplit? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FractionSplit Split based on fractions defining the size of each set.
---@field annotationSchemaUri? string Applicable only to custom training with Datasets that have DataItems and Annotations. Cloud Storage URI that points to a YAML file describing the annotation schema. The schema is defined as an OpenAPI 3.0.2 [Schema Object](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.0.2.md#schemaObject). The schema files that can be used here are found in gs://google-cloud-aiplatform/schema/dataset/annotation/ , note that the chosen schema must be consistent with metadata of the Dataset specified by dataset_id. Only Annotations that both match this schema and belong to DataItems not ignored by the split method are used in respectively training, validation or test role, depending on the role of the DataItem they are on. When used in conjunction with annotations_filter, the Annotations used for training are filtered by both annotations_filter and annotation_schema_uri.
---@field annotationsFilter? string Applicable only to Datasets that have DataItems and Annotations. A filter on Annotations of the Dataset. Only Annotations that both match this filter and belong to DataItems not ignored by the split method are used in respectively training, validation or test role, depending on the role of the DataItem they are on (for the auto-assigned that role is decided by Vertex AI). A filter with same syntax as the one used in ListAnnotations may be used, but note here it filters across all Annotations of the Dataset, and not just within a single DataItem.
---@field datasetId? string Required. The ID of the Dataset in the same Project and Location which data will be used to train the Model. The Dataset must use schema compatible with Model being trained, and what is compatible should be described in the used TrainingPipeline's training_task_definition. For tabular Datasets, all their data is exported to training, to pick and choose from.
---@field filterSplit? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FilterSplit Split based on the provided filters for each set.
---@field gcsDestination? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GcsDestination The Cloud Storage location where the training data is to be written to. In the given directory a new directory is created with name: `dataset---` where timestamp is in YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.sssZ ISO-8601 format. All training input data is written into that directory. The Vertex AI environment variables representing Cloud Storage data URIs are represented in the Cloud Storage wildcard format to support sharded data. e.g.: "gs://.../training-*.jsonl" * AIP_DATA_FORMAT = "jsonl" for non-tabular data, "csv" for tabular data * AIP_TRAINING_DATA_URI = "gcs_destination/dataset---/training-*.${AIP_DATA_FORMAT}" * AIP_VALIDATION_DATA_URI = "gcs_destination/dataset---/validation-*.${AIP_DATA_FORMAT}" * AIP_TEST_DATA_URI = "gcs_destination/dataset---/test-*.${AIP_DATA_FORMAT}"
---@field persistMlUseAssignment? boolean Whether to persist the ML use assignment to data item system labels.

---A list of int64 values.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Int64Array
---@field values? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList A list of int64 values.

---An attribution method that computes the Aumann-Shapley value taking advantage of the model's fully differentiable structure. Refer to this paper for more details: https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.01365
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IntegratedGradientsAttribution
---@field blurBaselineConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1BlurBaselineConfig Config for IG with blur baseline. When enabled, a linear path from the maximally blurred image to the input image is created. Using a blurred baseline instead of zero (black image) is motivated by the BlurIG approach explained here: https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.03383
---@field smoothGradConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1SmoothGradConfig Config for SmoothGrad approximation of gradients. When enabled, the gradients are approximated by averaging the gradients from noisy samples in the vicinity of the inputs. Adding noise can help improve the computed gradients. Refer to this paper for more details: https://arxiv.org/pdf/1706.03825.pdf
---@field stepCount? number Required. The number of steps for approximating the path integral. A good value to start is 50 and gradually increase until the sum to diff property is within the desired error range. Valid range of its value is [1, 100], inclusively.

---An extracted memory that is the intermediate result before consolidation.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IntermediateExtractedMemory
---@field fact? string Output only. Represents the fact of the extracted memory.
---@field structuredData? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentMap Output only. Represents the structured value of the extracted memory.
---@field context? string Output only. Represents the explanation of why the information was extracted from the source content.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IntermediateExtractedMemoryList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1IntermediateExtractedMemory[]

---The Jira source for the ImportRagFilesRequest.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1JiraSource
---@field jiraQueries? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1JiraSourceJiraQueriesList Required. The Jira queries.

---JiraQueries contains the Jira queries and corresponding authentication.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1JiraSourceJiraQueries
---@field projects? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList A list of Jira projects to import in their entirety.
---@field email? string Required. The Jira email address.
---@field customQueries? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList A list of custom Jira queries to import. For information about JQL (Jira Query Language), see https://support.atlassian.com/jira-service-management-cloud/docs/use-advanced-search-with-jira-query-language-jql/
---@field apiKeyConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ApiAuthApiKeyConfig Required. The SecretManager secret version resource name (e.g. projects/{project}/secrets/{secret}/versions/{version}) storing the Jira API key. See [Manage API tokens for your Atlassian account](https://support.atlassian.com/atlassian-account/docs/manage-api-tokens-for-your-atlassian-account/).
---@field serverUri? string Required. The Jira server URI.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1JiraSourceJiraQueriesList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1JiraSourceJiraQueries[]

---Represents the configuration for keep-alive probe. Contains configuration on a specified endpoint that a deployment host should use to keep the container alive based on the probe settings.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1KeepAliveProbe
---@field httpGet? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1KeepAliveProbeHttpGet Optional. Specifies the HTTP GET configuration for the probe.
---@field maxSeconds? number Optional. Specifies the maximum duration (in seconds) to keep the instance alive via this probe. Can be a maximum of 3600 seconds (1 hour).

---Specifies the HTTP GET configuration for the probe.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1KeepAliveProbeHttpGet
---@field path? string Required. Specifies the path of the HTTP GET request (e.g., `"/is_busy"`).
---@field port? number Optional. Specifies the port number on the container to which the request is sent.

---Specification for an LLM based metric.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1LLMBasedMetricSpec
---@field resultParserConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationParserConfig Optional. The parser config for the metric result.
---@field additionalConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentMap Optional. Optional additional configuration for the metric.
---@field systemInstruction? string Optional. System instructions for the judge model.
---@field predefinedRubricGenerationSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PredefinedMetricSpec Dynamically generate rubrics using a predefined spec.
---@field rubricGroupKey? string Use a pre-defined group of rubrics associated with the input. Refers to a key in the rubric_groups map of EvaluationInstance.
---@field judgeAutoraterConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AutoraterConfig Optional. Optional configuration for the judge LLM (Autorater).
---@field rubricGenerationSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RubricGenerationSpec Dynamically generate rubrics using this specification.
---@field metricPromptTemplate? string Required. Template for the prompt sent to the judge model.

---Contains information about the Large Model.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1LargeModelReference
---@field name? string Required. The unique name of the large Foundation or pre-built model. Like "chat-bison", "text-bison". Or model name with version ID, like "chat-bison@001", "text-bison@005", etc.

---A subgraph of the overall lineage graph. Event edges connect Artifact and Execution nodes.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1LineageSubgraph
---@field artifacts? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ArtifactList The Artifact nodes in the subgraph.
---@field events? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EventList The Event edges between Artifacts and Executions in the subgraph.
---@field executions? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ExecutionList The Execution nodes in the subgraph.

