---A query to find a number of similar entities.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQuery
---@field neighborCount? number Optional. The number of similar entities to be retrieved from feature view for each query.
---@field perCrowdingAttributeNeighborCount? number Optional. Crowding is a constraint on a neighbor list produced by nearest neighbor search requiring that no more than sper_crowding_attribute_neighbor_count of the k neighbors returned have the same value of crowding_attribute. It's used for improving result diversity.
---@field embedding? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryEmbedding Optional. The embedding vector that be used for similar search.
---@field parameters? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryParameters Optional. Parameters that can be set to tune query on the fly.
---@field numericFilters? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryNumericFilterList Optional. The list of numeric filters.
---@field stringFilters? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryStringFilterList Optional. The list of string filters.
---@field entityId? string Optional. The entity id whose similar entities should be searched for. If embedding is set, search will use embedding instead of entity_id.

---The embedding vector.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryEmbedding
---@field value? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DoubleList Optional. Individual value in the embedding.

---Numeric filter is used to search a subset of the entities by using boolean rules on numeric columns. For example: Database Point 0: {name: "a" value_int: 42} {name: "b" value_float: 1.0} Database Point 1: {name: "a" value_int: 10} {name: "b" value_float: 2.0} Database Point 2: {name: "a" value_int: -1} {name: "b" value_float: 3.0} Query: {name: "a" value_int: 12 operator: LESS} // Matches Point 1, 2 {name: "b" value_float: 2.0 operator: EQUAL} // Matches Point 1
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryNumericFilter
---@field valueDouble? number double value type.
---@field valueFloat? number float value type.
---@field name? string Required. Column name in BigQuery that used as filters.
---@field valueInt? string int value type.
---@field op? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryNumericFilterOpEnum|string Optional. This MUST be specified for queries and must NOT be specified for database points.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryNumericFilterList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryNumericFilter[]

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryNumericFilterOpEnum "OPERATOR_UNSPECIFIED"|"LESS"|"LESS_EQUAL"|"EQUAL"|"GREATER_EQUAL"|"GREATER"|"NOT_EQUAL"

---Parameters that can be overrided in each query to tune query latency and recall.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryParameters
---@field approximateNeighborCandidates? number Optional. The number of neighbors to find via approximate search before exact reordering is performed; if set, this value must be > neighbor_count.
---@field leafNodesSearchFraction? number Optional. The fraction of the number of leaves to search, set at query time allows user to tune search performance. This value increase result in both search accuracy and latency increase. The value should be between 0.0 and 1.0.

---String filter is used to search a subset of the entities by using boolean rules on string columns. For example: if a query specifies string filter with 'name = color, allow_tokens = {red, blue}, deny_tokens = {purple}',' then that query will match entities that are red or blue, but if those points are also purple, then they will be excluded even if they are red/blue. Only string filter is supported for now, numeric filter will be supported in the near future.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryStringFilter
---@field allowTokens? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. The allowed tokens.
---@field denyTokens? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. The denied tokens.
---@field name? string Required. Column names in BigQuery that used as filters.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryStringFilterList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborQueryStringFilter[]

---Nearest neighbors for one query.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighbors
---@field neighbors? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborsNeighborList All its neighbors.

---A neighbor of the query vector.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborsNeighbor
---@field entityId? string The id of the similar entity.
---@field distance? number The distance between the neighbor and the query vector.
---@field entityKeyValues? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1FetchFeatureValuesResponse The attributes of the neighbor, e.g. filters, crowding and metadata Note that full entities are returned only when "return_full_entity" is set to true. Otherwise, only the "entity_id" and "distance" fields are populated.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborsNeighborList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NearestNeighborsNeighbor[]

---Neighbors for example-based explanations.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Neighbor
---@field neighborId? string Output only. The neighbor id.
---@field neighborDistance? number Output only. The neighbor distance.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NeighborList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Neighbor[]

---Network spec.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NetworkSpec
---@field subnetwork? string The name of the subnet that this instance is in. Format: `projects/{project_id_or_number}/regions/{region}/subnetworks/{subnetwork_id}`
---@field enableInternetAccess? boolean Whether to enable public internet access. Default false.
---@field network? string The full name of the Google Compute Engine [network](https://cloud.google.com//compute/docs/networks-and-firewalls#networks)

---Represents a mount configuration for Network File System (NFS) to mount.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NfsMount
---@field path? string Required. Source path exported from NFS server. Has to start with '/', and combined with the ip address, it indicates the source mount path in the form of `server:path`
---@field server? string Required. IP address of the NFS server.
---@field mountPoint? string Required. Destination mount path. The NFS will be mounted for the user under /mnt/nfs/

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NfsMountList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NfsMount[]

---The euc configuration of NotebookRuntimeTemplate.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookEucConfig
---@field bypassActasCheck? boolean Output only. Whether ActAs check is bypassed for service account attached to the VM. If false, we need ActAs check for the default Compute Engine Service account. When a Runtime is created, a VM is allocated using Default Compute Engine Service Account. Any user requesting to use this Runtime requires Service Account User (ActAs) permission over this SA. If true, Runtime owner is using EUC and does not require the above permission as VM no longer use default Compute Engine SA, but a P4SA.
---@field eucDisabled? boolean Input only. Whether EUC is disabled in this NotebookRuntimeTemplate. In proto3, the default value of a boolean is false. In this way, by default EUC will be enabled for NotebookRuntimeTemplate.

---NotebookExecutionJob represents an instance of a notebook execution.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJob
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key spec for the notebook execution job. This field is auto-populated if the NotebookRuntimeTemplate has an encryption spec.
---@field notebookRuntimeTemplateResourceName? string The NotebookRuntimeTemplate to source compute configuration from.
---@field status? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Populated when the NotebookExecutionJob is completed. When there is an error during notebook execution, the error details are populated.
---@field serviceAccount? string The service account to run the execution as.
---@field executionTimeout? string Max running time of the execution job in seconds (default 86400s / 24 hrs).
---@field displayName? string The display name of the NotebookExecutionJob. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field workbenchRuntime? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobWorkbenchRuntime The Workbench runtime configuration to use for the notebook execution.
---@field customEnvironmentSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobCustomEnvironmentSpec The custom compute configuration for an execution job.
---@field executionUser? string The user email to run the execution as. Only supported by Colab runtimes.
---@field scheduleResourceName? string The Schedule resource name if this job is triggered by one. Format: `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}/schedules/{schedule_id}`
---@field dataformRepositorySource? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobDataformRepositorySource The Dataform Repository pointing to a single file notebook repository.
---@field jobState? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobJobStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the NotebookExecutionJob.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this NotebookExecutionJob was most recently updated.
---@field gcsOutputUri? string The Cloud Storage location to upload the result to. Format: `gs://bucket-name`
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of this NotebookExecutionJob. Format: `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}/notebookExecutionJobs/{job_id}`
---@field gcsNotebookSource? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobGcsNotebookSource The Cloud Storage url pointing to the ipynb file. Format: `gs://bucket/notebook_file.ipynb`
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize NotebookExecutionJobs. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable.
---@field directNotebookSource? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobDirectNotebookSource The contents of an input notebook file.
---@field kernelName? string The name of the kernel to use during notebook execution. If unset, the default kernel is used.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this NotebookExecutionJob was created.

---Compute configuration to use for an execution job.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobCustomEnvironmentSpec
---@field shieldedInstanceConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobCustomEnvironmentSpecShieldedInstanceConfig Optional. Shielded VM configuration (for example, Secure Boot) for the execution VM.
---@field machineSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1MachineSpec The specification of a single machine for the execution job.
---@field networkSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NetworkSpec The network configuration to use for the execution job.
---@field persistentDiskSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PersistentDiskSpec The specification of a persistent disk to attach for the execution job.

---A set of Shielded VM options for the execution VM. Mirrors `google.cloud.notebooks.v2.ShieldedInstanceConfig`. See https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/modifying-shielded-vm.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobCustomEnvironmentSpecShieldedInstanceConfig
---@field enableIntegrityMonitoring? boolean Optional. Whether the VM instance has integrity monitoring enabled.
---@field enableSecureBoot? boolean Optional. Whether the VM instance has Secure Boot enabled. Disabled by default.
---@field enableVtpm? boolean Optional. Whether the VM instance has vTPM enabled.

---The Dataform Repository containing the input notebook.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobDataformRepositorySource
---@field dataformRepositoryResourceName? string The resource name of the Dataform Repository. Format: `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}/repositories/{repository_id}`
---@field commitSha? string The commit SHA to read repository with. If unset, the file will be read at HEAD.

---The content of the input notebook in ipynb format.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobDirectNotebookSource
---@field content? string The base64-encoded contents of the input notebook file.

---The Cloud Storage uri for the input notebook.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobGcsNotebookSource
---@field uri? string The Cloud Storage uri pointing to the ipynb file. Format: `gs://bucket/notebook_file.ipynb`
---@field generation? string The version of the Cloud Storage object to read. If unset, the current version of the object is read. See https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/metadata#generation-number.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobJobStateEnum "JOB_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"JOB_STATE_QUEUED"|"JOB_STATE_PENDING"|"JOB_STATE_RUNNING"|"JOB_STATE_SUCCEEDED"|"JOB_STATE_FAILED"|"JOB_STATE_CANCELLING"|"JOB_STATE_CANCELLED"|"JOB_STATE_PAUSED"|"JOB_STATE_EXPIRED"|"JOB_STATE_UPDATING"|"JOB_STATE_PARTIALLY_SUCCEEDED"

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJob[]

---Configuration for a Workbench Instances-based environment.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobWorkbenchRuntime
---@field vmImage? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobWorkbenchRuntimeVmImage A specific Compute Engine VM image to run the notebook on.
---@field customContainerImage? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobWorkbenchRuntimeContainerImage A user-provided container image. The notebook executes inside this container on a managed container-host (COS) VM.

---The definition of a user-provided container image to run the notebook execution in. Mirrors `google.cloud.notebooks.v2.ContainerImage`.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobWorkbenchRuntimeContainerImage
---@field tag? string Optional. The tag of the container image. If unset, defaults to `latest`.
---@field repository? string Required. The path to the container image repository. For example: `gcr.io/{project_id}/{image_name}`.

---The definition of a Compute Engine VM image to run the notebook execution on. Mirrors `google.cloud.notebooks.v2.VmImage`.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookExecutionJobWorkbenchRuntimeVmImage
---@field name? string Use this VM image name to find the image.
---@field family? string Use this VM image family to find the image; the newest image in this family is used.
---@field project? string Required. The name of the Google Cloud project that this VM image belongs to. Format: `{project_id}`.

---The idle shutdown configuration of NotebookRuntimeTemplate, which contains the idle_timeout as required field.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookIdleShutdownConfig
---@field idleShutdownDisabled? boolean Whether Idle Shutdown is disabled in this NotebookRuntimeTemplate.
---@field idleTimeout? string Required. Duration is accurate to the second. In Notebook, Idle Timeout is accurate to minute so the range of idle_timeout (second) is: 10 * 60 ~ 1440 * 60.

---Notebook Reservation Affinity for consuming Zonal reservation.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookReservationAffinity
---@field consumeReservationType? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookReservationAffinityConsumeReservationTypeEnum|string Required. Specifies the type of reservation from which this instance can consume resources: RESERVATION_ANY (default), RESERVATION_SPECIFIC, or RESERVATION_NONE. See Consuming reserved instances for examples.
---@field values? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. Corresponds to the label values of a reservation resource. This must be the full path name of Reservation.
---@field key? string Optional. Corresponds to the label key of a reservation resource. To target a RESERVATION_SPECIFIC by name, use compute.googleapis.com/reservation-name as the key and specify the name of your reservation as its value.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookReservationAffinityConsumeReservationTypeEnum "RESERVATION_AFFINITY_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"RESERVATION_NONE"|"RESERVATION_ANY"|"RESERVATION_SPECIFIC"

---A runtime is a virtual machine allocated to a particular user for a particular Notebook file on temporary basis with lifetime. Default runtimes have a lifetime of 18 hours, while custom runtimes last for 6 months from their creation or last upgrade.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntime
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this NotebookRuntime was created.
---@field shieldedVmConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ShieldedVmConfig Output only. Runtime Shielded VM spec.
---@field description? string The description of the NotebookRuntime.
---@field notebookRuntimeTemplateRef? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeTemplateRef Output only. The pointer to NotebookRuntimeTemplate this NotebookRuntime is created from.
---@field runtimeState? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeRuntimeStateEnum|string Output only. The runtime (instance) state of the NotebookRuntime.
---@field healthState? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeHealthStateEnum|string Output only. The health state of the NotebookRuntime.
---@field reservationAffinity? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookReservationAffinity Output only. Reservation Affinity of the notebook runtime.
---@field idleShutdownConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookIdleShutdownConfig Output only. The idle shutdown configuration of the notebook runtime.
---@field machineSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1MachineSpec Output only. The specification of a single machine used by the notebook runtime.
---@field networkTags? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. The Compute Engine tags to add to runtime (see [Tagging instances](https://cloud.google.com/vpc/docs/add-remove-network-tags)).
---@field notebookRuntimeType? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeNotebookRuntimeTypeEnum|string Output only. The type of the notebook runtime.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the NotebookRuntime. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field serviceAccount? string Output only. Deprecated: This field is no longer used and the "Vertex AI Notebook Service Account" (service-PROJECT_NUMBER@gcp-sa-aiplatform-vm.iam.gserviceaccount.com) is used for the runtime workload identity. See https://cloud.google.com/iam/docs/service-agents#vertex-ai-notebook-service-account for more details. The service account that the NotebookRuntime workload runs as.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the NotebookRuntime.
---@field softwareConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookSoftwareConfig Output only. Software config of the notebook runtime.
---@field dataPersistentDiskSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PersistentDiskSpec Output only. The specification of persistent disk attached to the notebook runtime as data disk storage.
---@field expirationTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this NotebookRuntime will be expired: 1. System Predefined NotebookRuntime: 24 hours after creation. After expiration, system predifined runtime will be deleted. 2. User created NotebookRuntime: 6 months after last upgrade. After expiration, user created runtime will be stopped and allowed for upgrade.
---@field isUpgradable? boolean Output only. Whether NotebookRuntime is upgradable.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this NotebookRuntime was most recently updated.
---@field networkSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NetworkSpec Output only. Network spec of the notebook runtime.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Output only. Customer-managed encryption key spec for the notebook runtime.
---@field version? string Output only. The VM os image version of NotebookRuntime.
---@field proxyUri? string Output only. The proxy endpoint used to access the NotebookRuntime.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your NotebookRuntime. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one NotebookRuntime (System labels are excluded). See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable. Following system labels exist for NotebookRuntime: * "aiplatform.googleapis.com/notebook_runtime_gce_instance_id": output only, its value is the Compute Engine instance id. * "aiplatform.googleapis.com/colab_enterprise_entry_service": its value is either "bigquery" or "vertex"; if absent, it should be "vertex". This is to describe the entry service, either BigQuery or Vertex.
---@field runtimeUser? string Required. The user email of the NotebookRuntime.
---@field eucConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookEucConfig Output only. EUC configuration of the notebook runtime.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeHealthStateEnum "HEALTH_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"HEALTHY"|"UNHEALTHY"

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntime[]

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeNotebookRuntimeTypeEnum "NOTEBOOK_RUNTIME_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"USER_DEFINED"|"ONE_CLICK"

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeRuntimeStateEnum "RUNTIME_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"RUNNING"|"BEING_STARTED"|"BEING_STOPPED"|"STOPPED"|"BEING_UPGRADED"|"ERROR"|"INVALID"

---A template that specifies runtime configurations such as machine type, runtime version, network configurations, etc. Multiple runtimes can be created from a runtime template.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeTemplate
---@field eucConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookEucConfig EUC configuration of the NotebookRuntimeTemplate.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the NotebookRuntimeTemplate. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field etag? string Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this NotebookRuntimeTemplate was created.
---@field machineSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1MachineSpec Optional. Immutable. The specification of a single machine for the template.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize the NotebookRuntimeTemplates. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field dataPersistentDiskSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PersistentDiskSpec Optional. The specification of persistent disk attached to the runtime as data disk storage.
---@field softwareConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookSoftwareConfig Optional. The notebook software configuration of the notebook runtime.
---@field networkTags? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. The Compute Engine tags to add to runtime (see [Tagging instances](https://cloud.google.com/vpc/docs/add-remove-network-tags)).
---@field idleShutdownConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookIdleShutdownConfig The idle shutdown configuration of NotebookRuntimeTemplate. This config will only be set when idle shutdown is enabled.
---@field isDefault? boolean Output only. Deprecated: This field has no behavior. Use notebook_runtime_type = 'ONE_CLICK' instead. The default template to use if not specified.
---@field reservationAffinity? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookReservationAffinity Optional. Reservation Affinity of the notebook runtime template.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this NotebookRuntimeTemplate was most recently updated.
---@field notebookRuntimeType? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeTemplateNotebookRuntimeTypeEnum Optional. Immutable. The type of the notebook runtime template.
---@field networkSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NetworkSpec Optional. Network spec.
---@field serviceAccount? string Deprecated: This field is ignored and the "Vertex AI Notebook Service Account" (service-PROJECT_NUMBER@gcp-sa-aiplatform-vm.iam.gserviceaccount.com) is used for the runtime workload identity. See https://cloud.google.com/iam/docs/service-agents#vertex-ai-notebook-service-account for more details. For NotebookExecutionJob, use NotebookExecutionJob.service_account instead. The service account that the runtime workload runs as. You can use any service account within the same project, but you must have the service account user permission to use the instance. If not specified, the [Compute Engine default service account](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/access/service-accounts#default_service_account) is used.
---@field shieldedVmConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ShieldedVmConfig Optional. Immutable. Runtime Shielded VM spec.
---@field description? string The description of the NotebookRuntimeTemplate.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key spec for the notebook runtime.
---@field name? string The resource name of the NotebookRuntimeTemplate.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeTemplateList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeTemplate[]

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeTemplateNotebookRuntimeTypeEnum "NOTEBOOK_RUNTIME_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"USER_DEFINED"|"ONE_CLICK"

---Points to a NotebookRuntimeTemplateRef.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookRuntimeTemplateRef
---@field notebookRuntimeTemplate? string Immutable. A resource name of the NotebookRuntimeTemplate.

---Notebook Software Config. This is passed to the backend when user makes software configurations in UI.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1NotebookSoftwareConfig
---@field env? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EnvVarList Optional. Environment variables to be passed to the container. Maximum limit is 100.
---@field postStartupScriptConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PostStartupScriptConfig Optional. Post startup script config.
---@field colabImage? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ColabImage Optional. Google-managed NotebookRuntime colab image.

---An OnlineEvaluator contains the configuration for an Online Evaluation.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluator
---@field config? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorConfig Required. Configuration for the OnlineEvaluator.
---@field stateDetails? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorStateDetailsList Output only. Contains additional information about the state of the OnlineEvaluator. This is used to provide more details in the event of a failure.
---@field agentResource? string Required. Immutable. The name of the agent that the OnlineEvaluator evaluates periodically. This value is used to filter the traces with a matching cloud.resource_id and link the evaluation results with relevant dashboards/UIs. This field is immutable. Once set, it cannot be changed.
---@field metricSources? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1MetricSourceList Required. A list of metric sources to be used for evaluating samples. At least one MetricSource must be provided. Right now, only predefined metrics and registered metrics are supported. Every registered metric must have `display_name` (or `title`) and `score_range` defined. Otherwise, the evaluations will fail. The maximum number of `metric_sources` is 25.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when the OnlineEvaluator was created.
---@field cloudObservability? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservability Data source for the OnlineEvaluator, based on Google Cloud Observability stack (Cloud Trace & Cloud Logging).
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the OnlineEvaluator. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/onlineEvaluators/{id}.
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorStateEnum Output only. The state of the OnlineEvaluator.
---@field displayName? string Optional. Human-readable name for the OnlineEvaluator. The name doesn't have to be unique. The name can consist of any UTF-8 characters. The maximum length is `63` characters. If the display name exceeds max characters, an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is returned.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when the OnlineEvaluator was last updated.

---Data source for the OnlineEvaluator, based on Google Cloud Observability stack (Cloud Trace & Cloud Logging).
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservability
---@field traceView? string Optional. Optional trace view that will be used to query traces. If empty, the `_AllSpans` view from `_Trace` US bucket will be used, i.e. `projects/{project_id}/locations/us/buckets/_Trace/datasets/Spans/views/_AllSpans`.
---@field openTelemetry? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityOpenTelemetry Data source follows OpenTelemetry convention.
---@field sessionScope? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilitySessionScope Scope online evaluation to OTel sessions (i.e. group of traces with the same conversation ID).
---@field traceScope? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityTraceScope Scope online evaluation to single traces.
---@field logView? string Optional. Optional log view that will be used to query logs. If empty, the project's default view (`projects/{project_id}`) will be used.

---Defines a predicate for filtering based on a numeric value.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityNumericPredicate
---@field comparisonOperator? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityNumericPredicateComparisonOperatorEnum|string Required. The comparison operator to apply.
---@field value? number Required. The value to compare against.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityNumericPredicateComparisonOperatorEnum "COMPARISON_OPERATOR_UNSPECIFIED"|"LESS"|"LESS_OR_EQUAL"|"EQUAL"|"NOT_EQUAL"|"GREATER_OR_EQUAL"|"GREATER"

---Configuration for data source following OpenTelemetry.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityOpenTelemetry
---@field semconvVersion? string Required. Defines which version OTel Semantic Convention the data follows. Can be "1.39.0" or newer.

---If chosen, the online evaluator will evaluate sessions matching specified `filter`. A session is a group of traces with a common `gen_ai.conversation.id`.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilitySessionScope
---@field filter? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilitySessionScopePredicateList Optional. A list of predicates to filter sessions. Multiple predicates are combined using AND. The maximum number of predicates is 10.
---@field inactivityTrigger? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilitySessionScopeInactivityTrigger Session is considered ready for evaluation when there are no new traces for a specified period of inactivity.

---Configuration for inactivity based session completion.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilitySessionScopeInactivityTrigger
---@field threshold? string Required. The amount of time that must pass with no new traces before a session is considered ready for evaluation. This is a required field if InactivityTrigger is used. The value must be a positive duration no greater than 7 days (604800 seconds).

---Defines a single filter predicate.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilitySessionScopePredicate
---@field duration? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityNumericPredicate Filter on the duration of a session (in seconds).
---@field modelCallErrors? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityNumericPredicate Filter on the number of LLM call errors within a session.
---@field toolCalls? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityNumericPredicate Filter on the number of underlying tool calls within a session.
---@field modelCalls? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityNumericPredicate Filter on the number of underlying LLM calls within a session.
---@field serviceVersion? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityStringPredicate Filter on the versions that served a session (`service.version` OTel resource attribute); matches if any of them is listed. At most one is allowed. On Vertex AI Agent Engine, this is the runtime revision id, currently set only for agents created via v1beta1.
---@field toolCallErrors? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityNumericPredicate Filter on the number of tool call errors within a session.
---@field totalTokenUsage? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityNumericPredicate Filter on the total token usage within a session.
---@field userTurns? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityNumericPredicate Filter on the number of user turns within a session.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilitySessionScopePredicateList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilitySessionScopePredicate[]

---Defines a predicate for filtering based on a string value.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityStringPredicate
---@field values? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Required. The values to match exactly (case-sensitive). Requires 1 to 20 values, each at most 128 characters long.

---If chosen, the online evaluator will evaluate single traces matching specified `filter`.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityTraceScope
---@field filter? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityTraceScopePredicateList Optional. A list of predicates to filter traces. Multiple predicates are combined using AND. The maximum number of predicates is 10.

---Defines a single filter predicate.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityTraceScopePredicate
---@field serviceVersion? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityStringPredicate Filter on the version that served a trace (`service.version` OTel resource attribute). At most one is allowed. On Vertex AI Agent Engine, this is the runtime revision id, currently set only for agents created via v1beta1.
---@field duration? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityNumericPredicate Filter on the duration of a trace (in seconds).
---@field totalTokenUsage? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityNumericPredicate Filter on the total token usage within a trace.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityTraceScopePredicateList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityTraceScopePredicate[]

---Configuration for sampling behavior of the OnlineEvaluator. The OnlineEvaluator runs at a fixed interval of 10 minutes.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorConfig
---@field randomSampling? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorConfigRandomSampling Random sampling method.
---@field maxEvaluatedSamplesPerRun? string Optional. The maximum number of evaluations to perform per run. If set to 0, the number is unbounded.

---Configuration for random sampling.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorConfigRandomSampling
---@field percentage? number Required. The percentage of traces to sample for evaluation. Must be an integer between `1` and `100`.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluator[]

---Contains additional information about the state of the OnlineEvaluator.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorStateDetails
---@field message? string Output only. Human-readable message describing the state of the OnlineEvaluator.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorStateDetailsList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorStateDetails[]

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OnlineEvaluatorStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ACTIVE"|"SUSPENDED"|"FAILED"|"WARNING"

---Config for evaluation output.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OutputConfig
---@field gcsDestination? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GcsDestination Cloud storage destination for evaluation output.

---Specifies the properties of a single field that are included in each generated synthetic example. This helps the model understand what kind of data to generate for each field.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OutputFieldSpec
---@field fieldType? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OutputFieldSpecFieldTypeEnum|string Optional. The data type of the field. Defaults to CONTENT if not set.
---@field guidance? string Optional. Specific instructions for the large language model on how to generate content for this particular field. While the LLM can sometimes infer content from the field name, providing explicit guidance is preferred. For example, for a field named "review", the guidance could be "A positive review about a coffee maker."
---@field fieldName? string Required. The name of this field in the generated synthetic data, such as "email_subject" or "customer_review".

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OutputFieldSpecFieldTypeEnum "FIELD_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CONTENT"|"TEXT"|"IMAGE"|"AUDIO"

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OutputFieldSpecList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OutputFieldSpec[]

---Describes the info for output of EvaluationService.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1OutputInfo
---@field gcsOutputDirectory? string Output only. The full path of the Cloud Storage directory created, into which the evaluation results and aggregation results are written.

---PSC config that is used to automatically create PSC endpoints in the user projects.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PSCAutomationConfig
---@field ipAddress? string Output only. IP address rule created by the PSC service automation.
---@field forwardingRule? string Output only. Forwarding rule created by the PSC service automation.
---@field network? string Required. The full name of the Google Compute Engine [network](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/networks-and-firewalls#networks). [Format](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/reference/rest/v1/networks/get): `projects/{project}/global/networks/{network}`.
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PSCAutomationConfigStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the PSC service automation.
---@field projectId? string Required. Project id used to create forwarding rule.
---@field errorMessage? string Output only. Error message if the PSC service automation failed.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PSCAutomationConfigList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PSCAutomationConfig[]

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PSCAutomationConfigStateEnum "PSC_AUTOMATION_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PSC_AUTOMATION_STATE_SUCCESSFUL"|"PSC_AUTOMATION_STATE_FAILED"

---Input for pairwise metric.
