---Represents the spec of persistent disk and hyperdisk options.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PersistentDiskSpec
---@field diskSizeGb? string Size in GB of the disk (default is 100GB).
---@field diskType? string Type of the disk (default is "pd-standard"). Valid values: "pd-ssd" (Persistent Disk Solid State Drive) "pd-standard" (Persistent Disk Hard Disk Drive) "pd-balanced" (Balanced Persistent Disk) "pd-extreme" (Extreme Persistent Disk) "hyperdisk-balanced" (Hyperdisk Balanced) "hyperdisk-extreme" (Hyperdisk Extreme) "hyperdisk-balanced-high-availability" (Hyperdisk Balanced High Availability) "hyperdisk-ml" (Hyperdisk ML) "hyperdisk-throughput" (Hyperdisk Throughput)

---Represents long-lasting resources that are dedicated to users to runs custom workloads. A PersistentResource can have multiple node pools and each node pool can have its own machine spec.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PersistentResource
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when the PersistentResource was created.
---@field reservedIpRanges? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Optional. A list of names for the reserved IP ranges under the VPC network that can be used for this persistent resource. If set, we will deploy the persistent resource within the provided IP ranges. Otherwise, the persistent resource is deployed to any IP ranges under the provided VPC network. Example: ['vertex-ai-ip-range'].
---@field name? string Immutable. Resource name of a PersistentResource.
---@field error? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Only populated when persistent resource's state is `STOPPING` or `ERROR`.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The display name of the PersistentResource. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time when the PersistentResource was most recently updated.
---@field resourceRuntimeSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ResourceRuntimeSpec Optional. Persistent Resource runtime spec. For example, used for Ray cluster configuration.
---@field pscInterfaceConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PscInterfaceConfig Optional. Configuration for PSC-I for PersistentResource.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Optional. Customer-managed encryption key spec for a PersistentResource. If set, this PersistentResource and all sub-resources of this PersistentResource will be secured by this key.
---@field network? string Optional. The full name of the Compute Engine [network](/compute/docs/networks-and-firewalls#networks) to peered with Vertex AI to host the persistent resources. For example, `projects/12345/global/networks/myVPC`. [Format](/compute/docs/reference/rest/v1/networks/insert) is of the form `projects/{project}/global/networks/{network}`. Where {project} is a project number, as in `12345`, and {network} is a network name. To specify this field, you must have already [configured VPC Network Peering for Vertex AI](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/general/vpc-peering). If this field is left unspecified, the resources aren't peered with any network.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Time when the PersistentResource for the first time entered the `RUNNING` state.
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PersistentResourceStateEnum Output only. The detailed state of a Study.
---@field resourcePools? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ResourcePoolList Required. The spec of the pools of different resources.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap Optional. The labels with user-defined metadata to organize PersistentResource. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field resourceRuntime? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ResourceRuntime Output only. Runtime information of the Persistent Resource.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PersistentResourceList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PersistentResource[]

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PersistentResourceStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PROVISIONING"|"RUNNING"|"STOPPING"|"ERROR"|"REBOOTING"|"UPDATING"

---An instance of a machine learning PipelineJob.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJob
---@field jobDetail? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJobDetail Output only. The details of pipeline run. Not available in the list view.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this PipelineJob was most recently updated.
---@field pscInterfaceConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PscInterfaceConfig Optional. Configuration for PSC-I for PipelineJob.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the PipelineJob.
---@field pipelineSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentMap A compiled definition of a pipeline, represented as a `JSON` object. Defines the structure of the pipeline, including its components, tasks, and parameters. This specification is generated by compiling a pipeline function defined in `Python` using the `Kubeflow Pipelines SDK`.
---@field endTime? string Output only. Pipeline end time.
---@field preflightValidations? boolean Optional. Whether to do component level validations before job creation.
---@field reservedIpRanges? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList A list of names for the reserved ip ranges under the VPC network that can be used for this Pipeline Job's workload. If set, we will deploy the Pipeline Job's workload within the provided ip ranges. Otherwise, the job will be deployed to any ip ranges under the provided VPC network. Example: ['vertex-ai-ip-range'].
---@field displayName? string The display name of the Pipeline. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field error? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. The error that occurred during pipeline execution. Only populated when the pipeline's state is FAILED or CANCELLED.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Pipeline creation time.
---@field templateMetadata? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTemplateMetadata Output only. Pipeline template metadata. Will fill up fields if PipelineJob.template_uri is from supported template registry.
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJobStateEnum|string Output only. The detailed state of the job.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Pipeline start time.
---@field runtimeConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJobRuntimeConfig Runtime config of the pipeline.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize PipelineJob. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. Note there is some reserved label key for Vertex AI Pipelines. - `vertex-ai-pipelines-run-billing-id`, user set value will get overrided.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key spec for a pipelineJob. If set, this PipelineJob and all of its sub-resources will be secured by this key.
---@field network? string The full name of the Compute Engine [network](/compute/docs/networks-and-firewalls#networks) to which the Pipeline Job's workload should be peered. For example, `projects/12345/global/networks/myVPC`. [Format](/compute/docs/reference/rest/v1/networks/insert) is of the form `projects/{project}/global/networks/{network}`. Where {project} is a project number, as in `12345`, and {network} is a network name. Private services access must already be configured for the network. Pipeline job will apply the network configuration to the Google Cloud resources being launched, if applied, such as Vertex AI Training or Dataflow job. If left unspecified, the workload is not peered with any network.
---@field scheduleName? string Output only. The schedule resource name. Only returned if the Pipeline is created by Schedule API.
---@field templateUri? string A template uri from where the PipelineJob.pipeline_spec, if empty, will be downloaded. Currently, only uri from Vertex Template Registry & Gallery is supported. Reference to https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/pipelines/create-pipeline-template.
---@field serviceAccount? string The service account that the pipeline workload runs as. If not specified, the Compute Engine default service account in the project will be used. See https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/access/service-accounts#default_service_account Users starting the pipeline must have the `iam.serviceAccounts.actAs` permission on this service account.

---The runtime detail of PipelineJob.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJobDetail
---@field pipelineRunContext? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Context Output only. The context of the current pipeline run.
---@field pipelineContext? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Context Output only. The context of the pipeline.
---@field taskDetails? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailList Output only. The runtime details of the tasks under the pipeline.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJobList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJob[]

---The runtime config of a PipelineJob.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJobRuntimeConfig
---@field inputArtifacts? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJobRuntimeConfigInputArtifactMap The runtime artifacts of the PipelineJob. The key will be the input artifact name and the value would be one of the InputArtifact.
---@field parameterValues? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentMap The runtime parameters of the PipelineJob. The parameters will be passed into PipelineJob.pipeline_spec to replace the placeholders at runtime. This field is used by pipelines built using `PipelineJob.pipeline_spec.schema_version` 2.1.0, such as pipelines built using Kubeflow Pipelines SDK 1.9 or higher and the v2 DSL.
---@field parameters? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ValueMap Deprecated. Use RuntimeConfig.parameter_values instead. The runtime parameters of the PipelineJob. The parameters will be passed into PipelineJob.pipeline_spec to replace the placeholders at runtime. This field is used by pipelines built using `PipelineJob.pipeline_spec.schema_version` 2.0.0 or lower, such as pipelines built using Kubeflow Pipelines SDK 1.8 or lower.
---@field failurePolicy? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJobRuntimeConfigFailurePolicyEnum|string Represents the failure policy of a pipeline. Currently, the default of a pipeline is that the pipeline will continue to run until no more tasks can be executed, also known as PIPELINE_FAILURE_POLICY_FAIL_SLOW. However, if a pipeline is set to PIPELINE_FAILURE_POLICY_FAIL_FAST, it will stop scheduling any new tasks when a task has failed. Any scheduled tasks will continue to completion.
---@field gcsOutputDirectory? string Required. A path in a Cloud Storage bucket, which will be treated as the root output directory of the pipeline. It is used by the system to generate the paths of output artifacts. The artifact paths are generated with a sub-path pattern `{job_id}/{task_id}/{output_key}` under the specified output directory. The service account specified in this pipeline must have the `storage.objects.get` and `storage.objects.create` permissions for this bucket.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJobRuntimeConfigFailurePolicyEnum "PIPELINE_FAILURE_POLICY_UNSPECIFIED"|"PIPELINE_FAILURE_POLICY_FAIL_SLOW"|"PIPELINE_FAILURE_POLICY_FAIL_FAST"

---The type of an input artifact.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJobRuntimeConfigInputArtifact
---@field artifactId? string Artifact resource id from MLMD. Which is the last portion of an artifact resource name: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/metadataStores/default/artifacts/{artifact_id}`. The artifact must stay within the same project, location and default metadatastore as the pipeline.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJobRuntimeConfigInputArtifactMap { [string]: gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJobRuntimeConfigInputArtifact }

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineJobStateEnum "PIPELINE_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PIPELINE_STATE_QUEUED"|"PIPELINE_STATE_PENDING"|"PIPELINE_STATE_RUNNING"|"PIPELINE_STATE_SUCCEEDED"|"PIPELINE_STATE_FAILED"|"PIPELINE_STATE_CANCELLING"|"PIPELINE_STATE_CANCELLED"|"PIPELINE_STATE_PAUSED"

---The runtime detail of a task execution.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetail
---@field pipelineTaskStatus? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailPipelineTaskStatusList Output only. A list of task status. This field keeps a record of task status evolving over time.
---@field executorDetail? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskExecutorDetail Output only. The detailed execution info.
---@field outputs? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailArtifactListMap Output only. The runtime output artifacts of the task.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Task start time.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Task create time.
---@field error? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. The error that occurred during task execution. Only populated when the task's state is FAILED or CANCELLED.
---@field taskName? string Output only. The user specified name of the task that is defined in pipeline_spec.
---@field inputs? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailArtifactListMap Output only. The runtime input artifacts of the task.
---@field taskUniqueName? string Output only. The unique name of a task. This field is used by rerun pipeline job. Console UI and Vertex AI SDK will support triggering pipeline job reruns. The name is constructed by concatenating all the parent tasks name with the task name. For example, if a task named "child_task" has a parent task named "parent_task_1" and parent task 1 has a parent task named "parent_task_2", the task unique name will be "parent_task_2.parent_task_1.child_task".
---@field taskId? string Output only. The system generated ID of the task.
---@field parentTaskId? string Output only. The id of the parent task if the task is within a component scope. Empty if the task is at the root level.
---@field execution? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Execution Output only. The execution metadata of the task.
---@field endTime? string Output only. Task end time.
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailStateEnum|string Output only. State of the task.

---A list of artifact metadata.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailArtifactList
---@field artifacts? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ArtifactList Output only. A list of artifact metadata.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailArtifactListMap { [string]: gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailArtifactList }

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetail[]

---A single record of the task status.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailPipelineTaskStatus
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Update time of this status.
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailPipelineTaskStatusStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the task.
---@field error? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. The error that occurred during the state. May be set when the state is any of the non-final state (PENDING/RUNNING/CANCELLING) or FAILED state. If the state is FAILED, the error here is final and not going to be retried. If the state is a non-final state, the error indicates a system-error being retried.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailPipelineTaskStatusList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailPipelineTaskStatus[]

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailPipelineTaskStatusStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PENDING"|"RUNNING"|"SUCCEEDED"|"CANCEL_PENDING"|"CANCELLING"|"CANCELLED"|"FAILED"|"SKIPPED"|"NOT_TRIGGERED"

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskDetailStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PENDING"|"RUNNING"|"SUCCEEDED"|"CANCEL_PENDING"|"CANCELLING"|"CANCELLED"|"FAILED"|"SKIPPED"|"NOT_TRIGGERED"

---The runtime detail of a pipeline executor.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskExecutorDetail
---@field customJobDetail? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskExecutorDetailCustomJobDetail Output only. The detailed info for a custom job executor.
---@field containerDetail? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskExecutorDetailContainerDetail Output only. The detailed info for a container executor.

---The detail of a container execution. It contains the job names of the lifecycle of a container execution.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskExecutorDetailContainerDetail
---@field failedMainJobs? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Output only. The names of the previously failed CustomJob for the main container executions. The list includes the all attempts in chronological order.
---@field failedPreCachingCheckJobs? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Output only. The names of the previously failed CustomJob for the pre-caching-check container executions. This job will be available if the PipelineJob.pipeline_spec specifies the `pre_caching_check` hook in the lifecycle events. The list includes the all attempts in chronological order.
---@field mainJob? string Output only. The name of the CustomJob for the main container execution.
---@field preCachingCheckJob? string Output only. The name of the CustomJob for the pre-caching-check container execution. This job will be available if the PipelineJob.pipeline_spec specifies the `pre_caching_check` hook in the lifecycle events.

---The detailed info for a custom job executor.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTaskExecutorDetailCustomJobDetail
---@field failedJobs? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Output only. The names of the previously failed CustomJob. The list includes the all attempts in chronological order.
---@field job? string Output only. The name of the CustomJob.

---Pipeline template metadata if PipelineJob.template_uri is from supported template registry. Currently, the only supported registry is Artifact Registry.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PipelineTemplateMetadata
---@field version? string The version_name in artifact registry. Will always be presented in output if the PipelineJob.template_uri is from supported template registry. Format is "sha256:abcdef123456...".

---Input for pointwise metric.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PointwiseMetricInput
---@field metricSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PointwiseMetricSpec Required. Spec for pointwise metric.
---@field instance? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PointwiseMetricInstance Required. Pointwise metric instance.

---Pointwise metric instance. Usually one instance corresponds to one row in an evaluation dataset.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PointwiseMetricInstance
---@field contentMapInstance? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ContentMap Key-value contents for the mutlimodality input, including text, image, video, audio, and pdf, etc. The key is placeholder in metric prompt template, and the value is the multimodal content.
---@field jsonInstance? string Instance specified as a json string. String key-value pairs are expected in the json_instance to render PointwiseMetricSpec.instance_prompt_template.

---Spec for pointwise metric result.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PointwiseMetricResult
---@field explanation? string Output only. Explanation for pointwise metric score.
---@field score? number Output only. Pointwise metric score.
---@field customOutput? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1CustomOutput Output only. Spec for custom output.

---Spec for pointwise metric.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PointwiseMetricSpec
---@field customOutputFormatConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1CustomOutputFormatConfig Optional. CustomOutputFormatConfig allows customization of metric output. By default, metrics return a score and explanation. When this config is set, the default output is replaced with either: - The raw output string. - A parsed output based on a user-defined schema. If a custom format is chosen, the `score` and `explanation` fields in the corresponding metric result will be empty.
---@field metricPromptTemplate? string Required. Metric prompt template for pointwise metric.
---@field systemInstruction? string Optional. System instructions for pointwise metric.

---Represents a network port in a container.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Port
---@field containerPort? number The number of the port to expose on the pod's IP address. Must be a valid port number, between 1 and 65535 inclusive.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PortList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Port[]

---Post startup script config.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PostStartupScriptConfig
---@field postStartupScriptBehavior? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PostStartupScriptConfigPostStartupScriptBehaviorEnum|string Optional. Post startup script behavior that defines download and execution behavior.
---@field postStartupScript? string Optional. Post startup script to run after runtime is started.
---@field postStartupScriptUrl? string Optional. Post startup script url to download. Example: `gs://bucket/script.sh`

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PostStartupScriptConfigPostStartupScriptBehaviorEnum "POST_STARTUP_SCRIPT_BEHAVIOR_UNSPECIFIED"|"RUN_ONCE"|"RUN_EVERY_START"|"DOWNLOAD_AND_RUN_EVERY_START"

---A pre-tuned model for continuous tuning.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PreTunedModel
---@field tunedModelName? string The resource name of the Model. E.g., a model resource name with a specified version id or alias: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/models/{model}@{version_id}` `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/models/{model}@{alias}` Or, omit the version id to use the default version: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/models/{model}`
---@field baseModel? string Output only. The name of the base model this PreTunedModel was tuned from.
---@field checkpointId? string Optional. The source checkpoint id. If not specified, the default checkpoint will be used.

---Configuration for a prebuilt voice.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PrebuiltVoiceConfig
---@field voiceName? string The name of the prebuilt voice to use.

---The spec for a pre-defined metric.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PredefinedMetricSpec
---@field metricSpecName? string Required. The name of a pre-defined metric, such as "instruction_following_v1" or "text_quality_v1".
---@field metricSpecParameters? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentMap Optional. The parameters needed to run the pre-defined metric.

---Assigns input data to training, validation, and test sets based on the value of a provided key. Supported only for tabular Datasets.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PredefinedSplit
---@field key? string Required. The key is a name of one of the Dataset's data columns. The value of the key (either the label's value or value in the column) must be one of {`training`, `validation`, `test`}, and it defines to which set the given piece of data is assigned. If for a piece of data the key is not present or has an invalid value, that piece is ignored by the pipeline.

---Configuration for logging request-response to a BigQuery table.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PredictRequestResponseLoggingConfig
---@field bigqueryDestination? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1BigQueryDestination BigQuery table for logging. If only given a project, a new dataset will be created with name `logging__` where will be made BigQuery-dataset-name compatible (e.g. most special characters will become underscores). If no table name is given, a new table will be created with name `request_response_logging`
---@field enabled? boolean If logging is enabled or not.
---@field samplingRate? number Percentage of requests to be logged, expressed as a fraction in range(0,1].

---Response message for PredictionService.Predict.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PredictResponse
---@field deployedModelId? string ID of the Endpoint's DeployedModel that served this prediction.
---@field modelDisplayName? string Output only. The display name of the Model which is deployed as the DeployedModel that this prediction hits.
---@field predictions? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentList The predictions that are the output of the predictions call. The schema of any single prediction may be specified via Endpoint's DeployedModels' Model's PredictSchemata's prediction_schema_uri.
---@field model? string Output only. The resource name of the Model which is deployed as the DeployedModel that this prediction hits.
---@field metadata? any Output only. Request-level metadata returned by the model. The metadata type will be dependent upon the model implementation.
---@field modelVersionId? string Output only. The version ID of the Model which is deployed as the DeployedModel that this prediction hits.

---Contains the schemata used in Model's predictions and explanations via PredictionService.Predict, PredictionService.Explain and BatchPredictionJob.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PredictSchemata
---@field instanceSchemaUri? string Immutable. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing the format of a single instance, which are used in PredictRequest.instances, ExplainRequest.instances and BatchPredictionJob.input_config. The schema is defined as an OpenAPI 3.0.2 [Schema Object](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.0.2.md#schemaObject). AutoML Models always have this field populated by Vertex AI. Note: The URI given on output will be immutable and probably different, including the URI scheme, than the one given on input. The output URI will point to a location where the user only has a read access.
---@field predictionSchemaUri? string Immutable. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing the format of a single prediction produced by this Model, which are returned via PredictResponse.predictions, ExplainResponse.explanations, and BatchPredictionJob.output_config. The schema is defined as an OpenAPI 3.0.2 [Schema Object](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.0.2.md#schemaObject). AutoML Models always have this field populated by Vertex AI. Note: The URI given on output will be immutable and probably different, including the URI scheme, than the one given on input. The output URI will point to a location where the user only has a read access.
---@field parametersSchemaUri? string Immutable. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing the parameters of prediction and explanation via PredictRequest.parameters, ExplainRequest.parameters and BatchPredictionJob.model_parameters. The schema is defined as an OpenAPI 3.0.2 [Schema Object](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.0.2.md#schemaObject). AutoML Models always have this field populated by Vertex AI, if no parameters are supported, then it is set to an empty string. Note: The URI given on output will be immutable and probably different, including the URI scheme, than the one given on input. The output URI will point to a location where the user only has a read access.

---Statistics computed for datasets used for preference optimization.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PreferenceOptimizationDataStats
---@field tuningStepCount? string Output only. Number of tuning steps for this Tuning Job.
---@field droppedExampleIndices? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Output only. A partial sample of the indices (starting from 1) of the dropped examples.
---@field droppedExampleReasons? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Output only. For each index in `dropped_example_indices`, the user-facing reason why the example was dropped.
---@field scoreVariancePerExampleDistribution? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1DatasetDistribution Output only. Dataset distributions for scores variance per example.
---@field tuningDatasetExampleCount? string Output only. Number of examples in the tuning dataset.
---@field userDatasetExamples? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GeminiPreferenceExampleList Output only. Sample user examples in the training dataset.
---@field userOutputTokenDistribution? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1DatasetDistribution Output only. Dataset distributions for the user output tokens.
---@field userInputTokenDistribution? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1DatasetDistribution Output only. Dataset distributions for the user input tokens.
---@field scoresDistribution? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1DatasetDistribution Output only. Dataset distributions for scores.
---@field totalBillableTokenCount? string Output only. Number of billable tokens in the tuning dataset.

---Hyperparameters for Preference Optimization.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PreferenceOptimizationHyperParameters
---@field beta? number Optional. Weight for KL Divergence regularization.
---@field learningRateMultiplier? number Optional. Multiplier for adjusting the default learning rate.
---@field adapterSize? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PreferenceOptimizationHyperParametersAdapterSizeEnum|string Optional. Adapter size for preference optimization.
---@field epochCount? string Optional. Number of complete passes the model makes over the entire training dataset during training.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PreferenceOptimizationHyperParametersAdapterSizeEnum "ADAPTER_SIZE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ADAPTER_SIZE_ONE"|"ADAPTER_SIZE_TWO"|"ADAPTER_SIZE_FOUR"|"ADAPTER_SIZE_EIGHT"|"ADAPTER_SIZE_SIXTEEN"|"ADAPTER_SIZE_THIRTY_TWO"

---Tuning Spec for Preference Optimization.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PreferenceOptimizationSpec
---@field hyperParameters? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PreferenceOptimizationHyperParameters Optional. Hyperparameters for Preference Optimization.
---@field validationDatasetUri? string Optional. Cloud Storage path to file containing validation dataset for preference optimization tuning. The dataset must be formatted as a JSONL file.
---@field exportLastCheckpointOnly? boolean Optional. If set to true, disable intermediate checkpoints for Preference Optimization and only the last checkpoint will be exported. Otherwise, enable intermediate checkpoints for Preference Optimization. Default is false.
---@field trainingDatasetUri? string Required. Cloud Storage path to file containing training dataset for preference optimization tuning. The dataset must be formatted as a JSONL file.

---Preset configuration for example-based explanations
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Presets
---@field modality? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PresetsModalityEnum|string The modality of the uploaded model, which automatically configures the distance measurement and feature normalization for the underlying example index and queries. If your model does not precisely fit one of these types, it is okay to choose the closest type.
---@field query? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PresetsQueryEnum|string Preset option controlling parameters for speed-precision trade-off when querying for examples. If omitted, defaults to `PRECISE`.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PresetsModalityEnum "MODALITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"IMAGE"|"TEXT"|"TABULAR"

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PresetsQueryEnum "PRECISE"|"FAST"

---PrivateEndpoints proto is used to provide paths for users to send requests privately. To send request via private service access, use predict_http_uri, explain_http_uri or health_http_uri. To send request via private service connect, use service_attachment.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PrivateEndpoints
---@field serviceAttachment? string Output only. The name of the service attachment resource. Populated if private service connect is enabled.
---@field explainHttpUri? string Output only. Http(s) path to send explain requests.
---@field healthHttpUri? string Output only. Http(s) path to send health check requests.
---@field predictHttpUri? string Output only. Http(s) path to send prediction requests.

---Represents configuration for private service connect.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PrivateServiceConnectConfig
---@field projectAllowlist? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList A list of Projects from which the forwarding rule will target the service attachment.
---@field serviceAttachment? string Output only. The name of the generated service attachment resource. This is only populated if the endpoint is deployed with PrivateServiceConnect.
---@field enablePrivateServiceConnect? boolean Required. If true, expose the IndexEndpoint via private service connect.
---@field pscAutomationConfigs? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PSCAutomationConfigList Optional. List of projects and networks where the PSC endpoints will be created. This field is used by Online Inference(Prediction) only.

---Probe describes a health check to be performed against a container to determine whether it is alive or ready to receive traffic.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Probe
---@field grpc? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ProbeGrpcAction GrpcAction probes the health of a container by sending a gRPC request.
---@field successThreshold? number Number of consecutive successes before the probe is considered successful. Defaults to 1. Minimum value is 1. Maps to Kubernetes probe argument 'successThreshold'.
---@field exec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ProbeExecAction ExecAction probes the health of a container by executing a command.
---@field periodSeconds? number How often (in seconds) to perform the probe. Default to 10 seconds. Minimum value is 1. Must be less than timeout_seconds. Maps to Kubernetes probe argument 'periodSeconds'.
---@field httpGet? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ProbeHttpGetAction HttpGetAction probes the health of a container by sending an HTTP GET request.
---@field timeoutSeconds? number Number of seconds after which the probe times out. Defaults to 1 second. Minimum value is 1. Must be greater or equal to period_seconds. Maps to Kubernetes probe argument 'timeoutSeconds'.
---@field initialDelaySeconds? number Number of seconds to wait before starting the probe. Defaults to 0. Minimum value is 0. Maps to Kubernetes probe argument 'initialDelaySeconds'.
---@field failureThreshold? number Number of consecutive failures before the probe is considered failed. Defaults to 3. Minimum value is 1. Maps to Kubernetes probe argument 'failureThreshold'.
---@field tcpSocket? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ProbeTcpSocketAction TcpSocketAction probes the health of a container by opening a TCP socket connection.

---ExecAction specifies a command to execute.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ProbeExecAction
---@field command? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Command is the command line to execute inside the container, the working directory for the command is root ('/') in the container's filesystem. The command is simply exec'd, it is not run inside a shell, so traditional shell instructions ('|', etc) won't work. To use a shell, you need to explicitly call out to that shell. Exit status of 0 is treated as live/healthy and non-zero is unhealthy.

---GrpcAction checks the health of a container using a gRPC service.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ProbeGrpcAction
---@field port? number Port number of the gRPC service. Number must be in the range 1 to 65535.
---@field service? string Service is the name of the service to place in the gRPC HealthCheckRequest. See https://github.com/grpc/grpc/blob/master/doc/health-checking.md. If this is not specified, the default behavior is defined by gRPC.

---HttpGetAction describes an action based on HTTP Get requests.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ProbeHttpGetAction
---@field host? string Host name to connect to, defaults to the model serving container's IP. You probably want to set "Host" in httpHeaders instead.
---@field port? number Number of the port to access on the container. Number must be in the range 1 to 65535.
---@field path? string Path to access on the HTTP server.
---@field scheme? string Scheme to use for connecting to the host. Defaults to HTTP. Acceptable values are "HTTP" or "HTTPS".
---@field httpHeaders? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ProbeHttpHeaderList Custom headers to set in the request. HTTP allows repeated headers.

---HttpHeader describes a custom header to be used in HTTP probes
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ProbeHttpHeader
---@field value? string The header field value
---@field name? string The header field name. This will be canonicalized upon output, so case-variant names will be understood as the same header.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ProbeHttpHeaderList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ProbeHttpHeader[]

---TcpSocketAction probes the health of a container by opening a TCP socket connection.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ProbeTcpSocketAction
---@field host? string Optional: Host name to connect to, defaults to the model serving container's IP.
---@field port? number Number of the port to access on the container. Number must be in the range 1 to 65535.

---PscAutomatedEndpoints defines the output of the forwarding rule automatically created by each PscAutomationConfig.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PscAutomatedEndpoints
---@field matchAddress? string Ip Address created by the automated forwarding rule.
---@field projectId? string Corresponding project_id in pscAutomationConfigs
---@field network? string Corresponding network in pscAutomationConfigs.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PscAutomatedEndpointsList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PscAutomatedEndpoints[]

---Configuration for PSC-I.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PscInterfaceConfig
