---Specifies the parsing config for RagFiles.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagFileParsingConfig
---@field layoutParser? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagFileParsingConfigLayoutParser The Layout Parser to use for RagFiles.
---@field llmParser? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagFileParsingConfigLlmParser The LLM Parser to use for RagFiles.

---Document AI Layout Parser config.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagFileParsingConfigLayoutParser
---@field processorName? string The full resource name of a Document AI processor or processor version. The processor must have type `LAYOUT_PARSER_PROCESSOR`. If specified, the `additional_config.parse_as_scanned_pdf` field must be false. Format: * `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}/processors/{processor_id}` * `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}/processors/{processor_id}/processorVersions/{processor_version_id}`
---@field maxParsingRequestsPerMin? number The maximum number of requests the job is allowed to make to the Document AI processor per minute. Consult https://cloud.google.com/document-ai/quotas and the Quota page for your project to set an appropriate value here. If unspecified, a default value of 120 QPM would be used.

---Specifies the LLM parsing for RagFiles.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagFileParsingConfigLlmParser
---@field modelName? string The name of a LLM model used for parsing. Format: * `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}/publishers/{publisher}/models/{model}`
---@field maxParsingRequestsPerMin? number The maximum number of requests the job is allowed to make to the LLM model per minute. Consult https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/quotas and your document size to set an appropriate value here. If unspecified, a default value of 5000 QPM would be used.
---@field customParsingPrompt? string The prompt to use for parsing. If not specified, a default prompt will be used.

---Specifies the transformation config for RagFiles.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagFileTransformationConfig
---@field ragFileChunkingConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagFileChunkingConfig Specifies the chunking config for RagFiles.

---Configuration message for RagManagedDb used by RagEngine.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfig
---@field serverless? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfigServerless Sets the backend to be the serverless mode offered by RAG Engine.
---@field scaled? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfigScaled Deprecated: Use `mode` instead to set the tier under Spanner. Sets the RagManagedDb to the Scaled tier.
---@field unprovisioned? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfigUnprovisioned Deprecated: Use `mode` instead to set the tier under Spanner. Sets the RagManagedDb to the Unprovisioned tier.
---@field basic? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfigBasic Deprecated: Use `mode` instead to set the tier under Spanner. Sets the RagManagedDb to the Basic tier.
---@field spanner? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfigSpanner Sets the RAG Engine backend to be RagManagedDb, built on top of Spanner. NOTE: This is the default mode (w/ Basic Tier) if not explicitly chosen.

---Basic tier is a cost-effective and low compute tier suitable for the following cases: * Experimenting with RagManagedDb. * Small data size. * Latency insensitive workload. * Only using RAG Engine with external vector DBs. NOTE: This is the default tier under Spanner mode if not explicitly chosen.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfigBasic

---Scaled tier offers production grade performance along with autoscaling functionality. It is suitable for customers with large amounts of data or performance sensitive workloads.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfigScaled

---Message to configure the serverless mode offered by RAG Engine.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfigServerless

---Message to configure the Spanner database used by RagManagedDb.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfigSpanner
---@field scaled? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfigScaled Sets the RagManagedDb to the Scaled tier.
---@field basic? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfigBasic Sets the RagManagedDb to the Basic tier. This is the default tier for Spanner mode if not explicitly chosen.
---@field unprovisioned? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfigUnprovisioned Sets the RagManagedDb to the Unprovisioned tier.

---Disables the RAG Engine service and deletes all your data held within this service. This will halt the billing of the service. NOTE: Once deleted the data cannot be recovered. To start using RAG Engine again, you will need to update the tier by calling the UpdateRagEngineConfig API.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagManagedDbConfigUnprovisioned

