---Config for the Vector DB to use for RAG.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagVectorDbConfig
---@field vertexVectorSearch? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagVectorDbConfigVertexVectorSearch The config for the Vertex Vector Search.
---@field pinecone? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagVectorDbConfigPinecone The config for the Pinecone.
---@field ragManagedDb? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagVectorDbConfigRagManagedDb The config for the RAG-managed Vector DB.
---@field ragEmbeddingModelConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagEmbeddingModelConfig Optional. Immutable. The embedding model config of the Vector DB.
---@field apiAuth? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ApiAuth Authentication config for the chosen Vector DB.

---The config for the Pinecone.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagVectorDbConfigPinecone
---@field indexName? string Pinecone index name. This value cannot be changed after it's set.

---The config for the default RAG-managed Vector DB.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagVectorDbConfigRagManagedDb
---@field knn? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagVectorDbConfigRagManagedDbKNN Performs a KNN search on RagCorpus. Default choice if not specified.
---@field ann? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagVectorDbConfigRagManagedDbANN Performs an ANN search on RagCorpus. Use this if you have a lot of files (> 10K) in your RagCorpus and want to reduce the search latency.

---Config for ANN search. RagManagedDb uses a tree-based structure to partition data and facilitate faster searches. As a tradeoff, it requires longer indexing time and manual triggering of index rebuild via the ImportRagFiles and UpdateRagCorpus API.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagVectorDbConfigRagManagedDbANN
---@field treeDepth? number The depth of the tree-based structure. Only depth values of 2 and 3 are supported. Recommended value is 2 if you have if you have O(10K) files in the RagCorpus and set this to 3 if more than that. Default value is 2.
---@field leafCount? number Number of leaf nodes in the tree-based structure. Each leaf node contains groups of closely related vectors along with their corresponding centroid. Recommended value is 10 * sqrt(num of RagFiles in your RagCorpus). Default value is 500.

---Config for KNN search.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagVectorDbConfigRagManagedDbKNN

---The config for the Vertex Vector Search.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RagVectorDbConfigVertexVectorSearch
---@field indexEndpoint? string The resource name of the Index Endpoint. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/indexEndpoints/{index_endpoint}`
---@field index? string The resource name of the Index. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/indexes/{index}`

---Raw output.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RawOutput
---@field rawOutput? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringList Output only. Raw output string.

---Ray cluster level autoscaling configuration.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RayClusterAutoscalingSpec
---@field upscalingSpeed? string Optional. The number of nodes allowed to be pending as a multiple of the current number of nodes. [OSS Ray reference](https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/cluster/vms/user-guides/configuring-autoscaling.html#upscaling-and-downscaling-speed)
---@field idleTimeoutMinutes? string Optional. The number of minutes that need to pass before an idle worker node is removed by the autoscaler. Default is 5 mins.

---Configuration for the Ray OSS Logs.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RayLogsSpec
---@field disabled? boolean Optional. Flag to disable the export of Ray OSS logs to Cloud Logging.

---Configuration for the Ray metrics.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RayMetricSpec
---@field enableUsageStatsCollection? boolean Optional. Flag to enable the Ray usage stats collection by Anyscale. https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/cluster/usage-stats.html#usage-stats-collection Disable by default.
---@field disabled? boolean Optional. Flag to disable the Ray metrics collection.

---Configuration information for the Ray cluster. For experimental launch, Ray cluster creation and Persistent cluster creation are 1:1 mapping: We will provision all the nodes within the Persistent cluster as Ray nodes.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RaySpec
---@field rayLogsSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RayLogsSpec Optional. OSS Ray logging configurations.
---@field imageUri? string Optional. Default image for user to choose a preferred ML framework (for example, TensorFlow or Pytorch) by choosing from [Vertex prebuilt images](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/training/pre-built-containers). Either this or the resource_pool_images is required. Use this field if you need all the resource pools to have the same Ray image. Otherwise, use the {@code resource_pool_images} field.
---@field rayMetricSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RayMetricSpec Optional. Ray metrics configurations.
---@field resourcePoolImages? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap Optional. Required if image_uri isn't set. A map of resource_pool_id to prebuild Ray image if user need to use different images for different head/worker pools. This map needs to cover all the resource pool ids. Example: { "ray_head_node_pool": "head image" "ray_worker_node_pool1": "worker image" "ray_worker_node_pool2": "another worker image" }
---@field headNodeResourcePoolId? string Optional. This will be used to indicate which resource pool will serve as the Ray head node(the first node within that pool). Will use the machine from the first workerpool as the head node by default if this field isn't set.
---@field rayClusterAutoscalingSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1RayClusterAutoscalingSpec Optional. Optional Ray autoscaling configurations.

---Response message for FeaturestoreOnlineServingService.ReadFeatureValues.
