---ReasoningEngine provides a customizable runtime for models to determine which actions to take and in which order.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngine
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key spec for a ReasoningEngine. If set, this ReasoningEngine and all sub-resources of this ReasoningEngine will be secured by this key.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the ReasoningEngine. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}`
---@field spec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpec Optional. Configurations of the ReasoningEngine
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this ReasoningEngine was created.
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the ReasoningEngine.
---@field labels? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap Labels for the ReasoningEngine.
---@field contextSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineContextSpec Optional. Configuration for how Agent Engine sub-resources should manage context.
---@field etag? string Optional. Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the ReasoningEngine.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this ReasoningEngine was most recently updated.

---Configuration for how Agent Engine sub-resources should manage context.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineContextSpec
---@field memoryBankConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineContextSpecMemoryBankConfig Optional. Specification for a Memory Bank, which manages memories for the Agent Engine.

---Specification for a Memory Bank.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineContextSpecMemoryBankConfig
---@field generationConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineContextSpecMemoryBankConfigGenerationConfig Optional. Configuration for how to generate memories for the Memory Bank.
---@field ttlConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineContextSpecMemoryBankConfigTtlConfig Optional. Configuration for automatic TTL ("time-to-live") of the memories in the Memory Bank. If not set, TTL will not be applied automatically. The TTL can be explicitly set by modifying the `expire_time` of each Memory resource.
---@field customizationConfigs? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigList Optional. Configuration for how to customize Memory Bank behavior for a particular scope.
---@field disableMemoryRevisions? boolean If true, no memory revisions will be created for any requests to the Memory Bank.
---@field similaritySearchConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineContextSpecMemoryBankConfigSimilaritySearchConfig Optional. Configuration for how to perform similarity search on memories. If not set, the Memory Bank will use the default embedding model `text-embedding-005`.

---Configuration for how to generate memories.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineContextSpecMemoryBankConfigGenerationConfig
---@field model? string Optional. The model used to generate memories. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/google/models/{model}`.
---@field generationTriggerConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1MemoryGenerationTriggerConfig Optional. Specifies the default trigger configuration for generating memories using `IngestEvents`.

---Configuration for how to perform similarity search on memories.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineContextSpecMemoryBankConfigSimilaritySearchConfig
---@field embeddingModel? string Required. The model used to generate embeddings to lookup similar memories. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/google/models/{model}`.

---Configuration for automatically setting the TTL ("time-to-live") of the memories in the Memory Bank.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineContextSpecMemoryBankConfigTtlConfig
---@field memoryRevisionDefaultTtl? string Optional. The default TTL duration of the memory revisions in the Memory Bank. This applies to all operations that create a memory revision. If not set, a default TTL of 365 days will be used.
---@field defaultTtl? string Optional. The default TTL duration of the memories in the Memory Bank. This applies to all operations that create or update a memory.
---@field granularTtlConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineContextSpecMemoryBankConfigTtlConfigGranularTtlConfig Optional. The granular TTL configuration of the memories in the Memory Bank.

---Configuration for TTL of the memories in the Memory Bank based on the action that created or updated the memory.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineContextSpecMemoryBankConfigTtlConfigGranularTtlConfig
---@field createTtl? string Optional. The TTL duration for memories uploaded via CreateMemory.
---@field generateCreatedTtl? string Optional. The TTL duration for memories newly generated via GenerateMemories (GenerateMemoriesResponse.GeneratedMemory.Action.CREATED).
---@field generateUpdatedTtl? string Optional. The TTL duration for memories updated via GenerateMemories (GenerateMemoriesResponse.GeneratedMemory.Action.UPDATED). In the case of an UPDATE action, the `expire_time` of the existing memory will be updated to the new value (now + TTL).

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngine[]

---ReasoningEngine configurations
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpec
---@field agentFramework? string Optional. The OSS agent framework used to develop the agent. Currently supported values: "google-adk", "langchain", "langgraph", "ag2", "llama-index", "custom".
---@field classMethods? gcp.aiplatform_v1.DocumentMapList Optional. Declarations for object class methods in OpenAPI specification format.
---@field packageSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecPackageSpec Optional. User provided package spec of the ReasoningEngine. Ignored when users directly specify a deployment image through `deployment_spec.first_party_image_override`, but keeping the field_behavior to avoid introducing breaking changes. The `deployment_source` field should not be set if `package_spec` is specified.
---@field containerSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecContainerSpec Deploy from a container image with a defined entrypoint and commands.
---@field sourceCodeSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecSourceCodeSpec Deploy from source code files with a defined entrypoint.
---@field deploymentSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecDeploymentSpec Optional. The specification of a Reasoning Engine deployment.
---@field identityType? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecIdentityTypeEnum|string Optional. The identity type to use for the Reasoning Engine. If not specified, the `service_account` field will be used if set, otherwise the default Vertex AI Reasoning Engine Service Agent in the project will be used.
---@field buildSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecBuildSpec Optional. Configuration for building container image.
---@field serviceAccount? string Optional. The service account that the Reasoning Engine artifact runs as. It should have "roles/storage.objectViewer" for reading the user project's Cloud Storage and "roles/aiplatform.user" for using Vertex extensions. If not specified, the Vertex AI Reasoning Engine Service Agent in the project will be used.
---@field effectiveIdentity? string Output only. The identity to use for the Reasoning Engine. It can contain one of the following values: * service-{project}@gcp-sa-aiplatform-re.googleapis.com (for SERVICE_AGENT identity type) * {name}@{project}.gserviceaccount.com (for SERVICE_ACCOUNT identity type) * agents.global.{org}.system.id.goog/resources/aiplatform/projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine} (for AGENT_IDENTITY identity type)

---Specification for building container image.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecBuildSpec
---@field workerPool? string Optional. Identifier. The resource name of the Cloud Build WorkerPool to use for the build. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/workerPools/{worker_pool}`
---@field serviceAccount? string Optional. The service account that Cloud Build uses to run the build. This field is only applicable when `worker_pool` is specified (i.e., for custom worker pools). If `worker_pool` is not specified, this field is ignored and the build runs using the Google-managed service agent. Format: `projects/{project}/serviceAccounts/{service_account}` or `{service_account}@{project}.iam.gserviceaccount.com`

---Specification for deploying from a container image.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecContainerSpec
---@field imageUri? string Required. The Artifact Registry Docker image URI (e.g., us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/my-project/my-repo/my-image:tag) of the container image that is to be run on each worker replica.
---@field port? number Optional. The port the container listens on. Defaults to 8080 if unset.

---The specification of a Reasoning Engine deployment.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecDeploymentSpec
---@field secretEnv? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1SecretEnvVarList Optional. Environment variables where the value is a secret in Cloud Secret Manager. To use this feature, add 'Secret Manager Secret Accessor' role (roles/secretmanager.secretAccessor) to AI Platform Reasoning Engine Service Agent.
---@field resourceLimits? gcp.aiplatform_v1.StringMap Optional. Resource limits for each container. Only 'cpu' and 'memory' keys are supported. Defaults to {"cpu": "4", "memory": "4Gi"}. * The only supported values for CPU are '1', '2', '4', '6' and '8'. For more information, go to https://cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/cpu. * The only supported values for memory are '1Gi', '2Gi', ... '32 Gi'. * For required cpu on different memory values, go to https://cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/memory-limits
---@field containerConcurrency? number Optional. Concurrency for each container and agent server. Recommended value: 2 * cpu + 1. Defaults to 9.
---@field pscInterfaceConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1PscInterfaceConfig Optional. Configuration for PSC-I.
---@field env? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EnvVarList Optional. Environment variables to be set with the Reasoning Engine deployment. The environment variables can be updated through the UpdateReasoningEngine API.
---@field agentGatewayConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecDeploymentSpecAgentGatewayConfig Optional. Agent Gateway configuration for the Reasoning Engine deployment.
---@field keepAliveProbe? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1KeepAliveProbe Optional. Specifies the configuration for keep-alive probe. Contains configuration on a specified endpoint that a deployment host should use to keep the container alive based on the probe settings.
---@field minInstances? number Optional. The minimum number of application instances that will be kept running at all times. Defaults to 1. Range: [0, 75].
---@field maxInstances? number Optional. The maximum number of application instances that can be launched to handle increased traffic. Defaults to 100. Range: [1, 1000]. If VPC-SC or PSC-I is enabled, the acceptable range is [1, 100].

---Agent Gateway configuration for a Reasoning Engine deployment.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecDeploymentSpecAgentGatewayConfig
---@field agentToAnywhereConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecDeploymentSpecAgentGatewayConfigAgentToAnywhereConfig Optional. Configuration for traffic originating from the Reasoning Engine. When unset, outgoing traffic is not routed through an Agent Gateway.
---@field clientToAgentConfig? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecDeploymentSpecAgentGatewayConfigClientToAgentConfig Optional. Configuration for traffic targeting the Reasoning Engine. When unset, incoming traffic is not routed through an Agent Gateway.

---Configuration for traffic originating from a Reasoning Engine.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecDeploymentSpecAgentGatewayConfigAgentToAnywhereConfig
---@field agentGateway? string Required. The resource name of the Agent Gateway for outbound traffic. It must be set to a Google-managed gateway whose `governed_access_path` is `AGENT_TO_ANYWHERE`. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agentGateways/{agent_gateway}`

---Configuration for traffic targeting a Reasoning Engine.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecDeploymentSpecAgentGatewayConfigClientToAgentConfig
---@field agentGateway? string Required. The resource name of the Agent Gateway to use for inbound traffic. It must be set to a Google-managed gateway whose `governed_access_path` is `CLIENT_TO_AGENT`. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agentGateways/{agent_gateway}`

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecIdentityTypeEnum "IDENTITY_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SERVICE_ACCOUNT"|"AGENT_IDENTITY"

---User-provided package specification, containing pickled object and package requirements.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecPackageSpec
---@field requirementsGcsUri? string Optional. The Cloud Storage URI of the `requirements.txt` file
---@field pythonVersion? string Optional. The Python version. Supported values are 3.10, 3.11, 3.12, 3.13, 3.14. If not specified, the default value is 3.10.
---@field dependencyFilesGcsUri? string Optional. The Cloud Storage URI of the dependency files in tar.gz format.
---@field pickleObjectGcsUri? string Optional. The Cloud Storage URI of the pickled python object.

---Specification for deploying from source code.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecSourceCodeSpec
---@field agentConfigSource? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecSourceCodeSpecAgentConfigSource Source code is generated from the agent config.
---@field pythonSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecSourceCodeSpecPythonSpec Configuration for a Python application.
---@field imageSpec? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ReasoningEngineSpecSourceCodeSpecImageSpec Optional. Configuration for building an image with custom config file.
