---A SavedQuery is a view of the dataset. It references a subset of annotations by problem type and filters.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1SavedQuery
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the SavedQuery.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this SavedQuery was created.
---@field annotationFilter? string Output only. Filters on the Annotations in the dataset.
---@field annotationSpecCount? number Output only. Number of AnnotationSpecs in the context of the SavedQuery.
---@field supportAutomlTraining? boolean Output only. If the Annotations belonging to the SavedQuery can be used for AutoML training.
---@field etag? string Used to perform a consistent read-modify-write update. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field metadata? any Some additional information about the SavedQuery.
---@field displayName? string Required. The user-defined name of the SavedQuery. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field problemType? string Required. Problem type of the SavedQuery. Allowed values: * IMAGE_CLASSIFICATION_SINGLE_LABEL * IMAGE_CLASSIFICATION_MULTI_LABEL * IMAGE_BOUNDING_POLY * IMAGE_BOUNDING_BOX * TEXT_CLASSIFICATION_SINGLE_LABEL * TEXT_CLASSIFICATION_MULTI_LABEL * TEXT_EXTRACTION * TEXT_SENTIMENT * VIDEO_CLASSIFICATION * VIDEO_OBJECT_TRACKING
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when SavedQuery was last updated.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1SavedQueryList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1SavedQuery[]

---One point viewable on a scalar metric plot.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Scalar
---@field value? number Value of the point at this step / timestamp.

---An instance of a Schedule periodically schedules runs to make API calls based on user specified time specification and API request type.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Schedule
---@field maxConcurrentRunCount? string Required. Maximum number of runs that can be started concurrently for this Schedule. This is the limit for starting the scheduled requests and not the execution of the operations/jobs created by the requests (if applicable).
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was updated.
---@field name? string Immutable. The resource name of the Schedule.
---@field displayName? string Required. User provided name of the Schedule. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field catchUp? boolean Output only. Whether to backfill missed runs when the schedule is resumed from PAUSED state. If set to true, all missed runs will be scheduled. New runs will be scheduled after the backfill is complete. Default to false.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was created.
---@field lastScheduledRunResponse? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ScheduleRunResponse Output only. Response of the last scheduled run. This is the response for starting the scheduled requests and not the execution of the operations/jobs created by the requests (if applicable). Unset if no run has been scheduled yet.
---@field createNotebookExecutionJobRequest? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1CreateNotebookExecutionJobRequest Request for NotebookService.CreateNotebookExecutionJob.
---@field maxConcurrentActiveRunCount? string Optional. Specifies the maximum number of active runs that can be executed concurrently for this Schedule. This limits the number of runs that can be in a non-terminal state at the same time. Currently, this field is only supported for requests of type CreatePipelineJobRequest.
---@field cron? string Cron schedule (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cron) to launch scheduled runs. To explicitly set a timezone to the cron tab, apply a prefix in the cron tab: "CRON_TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}" or "TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}". The ${IANA_TIME_ZONE} may only be a valid string from IANA time zone database. For example, "CRON_TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *", or "TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *".
---@field endTime? string Optional. Timestamp after which no new runs can be scheduled. If specified, The schedule will be completed when either end_time is reached or when scheduled_run_count >= max_run_count. If not specified, new runs will keep getting scheduled until this Schedule is paused or deleted. Already scheduled runs will be allowed to complete. Unset if not specified.
---@field lastResumeTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was last resumed. Unset if never resumed from pause.
---@field maxRunCount? string Optional. Maximum run count of the schedule. If specified, The schedule will be completed when either started_run_count >= max_run_count or when end_time is reached. If not specified, new runs will keep getting scheduled until this Schedule is paused or deleted. Already scheduled runs will be allowed to complete. Unset if not specified.
---@field allowQueueing? boolean Optional. Whether new scheduled runs can be queued when max_concurrent_runs limit is reached. If set to true, new runs will be queued instead of skipped. Default to false.
---@field state? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ScheduleStateEnum Output only. The state of this Schedule.
---@field startTime? string Optional. Timestamp after which the first run can be scheduled. Default to Schedule create time if not specified.
---@field nextRunTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule should schedule the next run. Having a next_run_time in the past means the runs are being started behind schedule.
---@field startedRunCount? string Output only. The number of runs started by this schedule.
---@field lastPauseTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was last paused. Unset if never paused.
---@field createPipelineJobRequest? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1CreatePipelineJobRequest Request for PipelineService.CreatePipelineJob. CreatePipelineJobRequest.parent field is required (format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}).

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ScheduleList gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Schedule[]

---Status of a scheduled run.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ScheduleRunResponse
---@field runResponse? string The response of the scheduled run.
---@field scheduledRunTime? string The scheduled run time based on the user-specified schedule.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ScheduleStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ACTIVE"|"PAUSED"|"COMPLETED"

---All parameters related to queuing and scheduling of custom jobs.
---@class gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Scheduling
---@field disableRetries? boolean Optional. Indicates if the job should retry for internal errors after the job starts running. If true, overrides `Scheduling.restart_job_on_worker_restart` to false.
---@field strategy? gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1SchedulingStrategyEnum|string Optional. This determines which type of scheduling strategy to use.
---@field restartJobOnWorkerRestart? boolean Optional. Restarts the entire CustomJob if a worker gets restarted. This feature can be used by distributed training jobs that are not resilient to workers leaving and joining a job.
---@field maxWaitDuration? string Optional. This is the maximum duration that a job will wait for the requested resources to be provisioned if the scheduling strategy is set to [Strategy.DWS_FLEX_START]. If set to 0, the job will wait indefinitely. The default is 24 hours.
---@field timeout? string Optional. The maximum job running time. The default is 7 days.

---@alias gcp.aiplatform_v1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1SchedulingStrategyEnum "STRATEGY_UNSPECIFIED"|"ON_DEMAND"|"LOW_COST"|"STANDARD"|"SPOT"|"FLEX_START"

